            lines {
              text: "## 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 1 \342\200\224 Expo-Portable Clean Core inside a Live Vite Web/PWA App**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Build a full installable PWA (`vite-plugin-pwa`, manifest, maskable + iOS PNG icons, offline shell, in-app install button) while strictly isolating pure business logic, Zod schemas, cryptographic primitives, i18n bundles, and repository interfaces from React DOM or browser globals."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Delivers a genuinely testable, installable app today in this workspace while allowing the exact `domain/`, `schemas/`, and `repositories/` contracts to drop directly into an Expo SDK + EAS Dev Build repository when you build native Android/iOS binaries."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Authoring raw Expo/React Native native files here would fail to run in the browser preview and block live visual verification."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 2 \342\200\224 Spark Free Tier + Local-Only Document Vault First**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Use Cloud Firestore (with IndexedDB multi-tab offline persistence) for structured metadata and real-time cross-device sync, paired with a Local-Only Document Vault adapter backed by browser IndexedDB (and `expo-file-system` on native) behind a unified `VaultStorageAdapter` interface."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Cloud Storage for Firebase requires the Blaze billing plan. Starting with Local-Only Vault keeps Stage 0 strictly at $0 with zero billing risk while preserving a 1-line adapter swap to Cloud Storage when you enable Blaze later."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Requiring Blaze immediately adds billing setup friction before personal testing."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 3 \342\200\224 Server-Side Gemini Proxy Behind `LLMProvider` + Hard Privacy Gate**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: All AI calls route through a provider-agnostic `LLMProvider` interface to an Express server endpoint (`/api/ai/complete`) backed by the official `@google/genai` SDK (`gemini-4-hydrogen` primary, `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` lightweight/fallback, driven by configuration\342\200\224never hardcoded in UI). No API key ever reaches the browser. A strict client + server **Privacy Gate** blocks sensitive payloads (Vault files, IDs/passports, locked/E2E notes) whenever `free_tier = true`."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Guarantees zero secret exposure, supports future drop-in migration to a Firebase Cloud Function proxy (Vertex AI / Claude / OpenAI), enforces daily per-user quotas + response caching, and protects sensitive documents from free-tier data retention."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Direct client-side AI calls without a server proxy expose keys or tie the app rigidly to a single SDK."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 4 \342\200\224 Opt-In Client-Side E2E Encryption (AES-256-GCM + Recovery Key)**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Use standard Web Crypto API (`PBKDF2-SHA256` key derivation + `AES-256-GCM` authenticated encryption with per-item random 96-bit IVs) for opted-in Vault folders and locked notes, generating a human-readable Recovery Key stored only by the user."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Gives true zero-knowledge protection for passports, IDs, and private notes while keeping regular notes/tasks fast, searchable, and AI-compatible by default."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Always-on E2E breaks search and AI assistance across non-sensitive daily items and increases accidental data-loss risk if a user loses their passphrase."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 5 \342\200\224 Eight-Pillar Hardened Firestore Security Rules + Emulator TDD**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Author `firebase-blueprint.json`, `security_spec.md` (with Dirty Dozen adversarial payloads), `firestore.rules` (default deny, strict `uid == request.auth.uid`, `email_verified`, `isValidId()`, per-entity `isValid*()` helpers, immutable `createdAt`/`ownerId`, server-only lock on `entitlements/current`, monotonic daily `aiUsage`), lint with `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`, and ship automated unit tests verifying cross-user and schema-poisoning rejections."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Financial and identity metadata require verifiable, zero-trust enforcement at the database boundary rather than client-side filtering."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "## 4. Technical Architecture & Data Strategy *(Technical Reference)*"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "### System & Component Architecture"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "```text"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
