  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Firebase Configuration**\n\nI\'m pleased to share that the `ProvisionFirebase` step completed successfully, yielding the crucial `firebase-applet-config.json` file. My attention is now fully dedicated to meticulously reviewing the requirements documentation. Before embarking on any package installations or code implementation, I\'m taking the time to ensure a comprehensive understanding of all aspects.\n\n\n**Analyzing Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve carefully examined the `environment_constraints` to ensure efficient package installation. My focus is on creating a single, batched `install_applet_package` call that lists all Phase 1 runtime and `@types/*` packages together, following the spec exactly. I\'ve compiled a definitive list: `firebase`, `zustand`, `zod`, `i18next`, `react-i18next`, `vite-plugin-pwa`, and `@google/genai@latest`. I will use `replace_file_content` for any `package.json` modifications.\n\n\n**Confirming Package Integration**\n\nI\'m thrilled to confirm that all required packages, including those for security and Google AI, can be installed within a *single*, non-dev dependency `install_applet_package` call. The inclusion of `@google/genai@latest` addresses compatibility requirements for the latest Gemini models. I\'ve also verified the inclusion of `eslint` and `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules` to lint the security rules. I\'m excited about this efficient integration. Now to consider the next steps... I will handle `package.json` modifications next!\n\n\n**Verifying Workspace Readiness**\n\nI\'m now formulating the Ultra-Mode verification plan. First, I\'ll need to check the `SKILL.md` file within the `ultra_mode` directory, and potentially explore the `computer-use` skill. I will prioritize checking `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`, if available. I\'ll need to do this concurrently with package installation, to stay efficient. This will then inform the journeys I need to verify in Phase 1, like Offline/Demo readiness.\n\n\n**Testing Localization Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying language switching and RTL layout. I\'ll test English, Arabic, and Kurdish Sorani, ensuring proper mirroring and currency formatting for both IQD and USD. Following this, I\'ll move on to the Ultra-Mode security journey.\n\n**Verifying Ultra-Mode Features**\n\nI am now formulating tests for the Ultra-Mode security features. I plan to configure PIN App Lock, initialize the Opt-In E2E Vault, and test encrypt/decrypt functionality. I will also test the Privacy Gate with sensitive and safe AI queries to verify its blocking behavior and Zod validation. Finally, I\'ll write and run unit tests for currency formatting and the AI privacy gate.\n\n\n**Implementing Security Rules**\n\nI am now focused on security. I\'ll meticulously craft the security rules, adhering strictly to `firebase-blueprint.json` and `security_spec.md`, and write `firestore.rules.test.ts`. I will also use `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules` to lint `DRAFT_firestore.rules`, and audit and patch to finalize the rules, before deployment via `rpc_action`. In parallel, I\'ll update `metadata.json` and `index.html`.\n\n\n"
