  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Validating Rules & Deploying**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The ESLint check on `firestore.rules` passed cleanly \342\200\223 zero errors, zero warnings. Now, I\'m deploying the rules immediately using `rpc_action`, calling \"fax\" service\'s \"DeployRules\" method. Simultaneously, I\'m getting started on the **Expo-portable Pure Core** modules, along with their `node:test` unit tests.\n\n\n**Designing Core Modules**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the Expo-portable `src/core/` modules. I\'m focusing on clean design \342\200\223 pure TypeScript with no React DOM or Firebase SDK imports. I\'ve started with `currency.ts` and `ai/privacyGate.ts`. Next I\'m tackling `e2eCrypto.ts`. I want to cover currency formatting, AI privacy checks, and end-to-end encryption. I will be sure to add unit tests for each module, as well.\n\n\n"
