  planner_response {
    response: "### Phase 1 Complete \342\200\224 LifeOS Foundation\n\n#### What Was Built\n- **Firebase & Offline-First Sync**: Provisioned Firebase Auth (Google Sign-In; Apple Sign-In isolated behind `auth.apple.enabled = false`) and Cloud Firestore with multi-tab IndexedDB persistent local cache, startup connectivity validation, and structured permission error handling behind a platform-agnostic repository layer (`AuthRepository`, `UserProfileRepository`, `AiUsageRepository`, `LocalVaultStorageAdapter`).\n- **Hardened Security Rules & Blueprint**: Authored the JSON Schema data blueprint, security test specification, composite indexes, and deployed Eight-Pillar `firestore.rules` (strict per-user tenant isolation under `users/{uid}/...`, `email_verified` enforcement, server-only lock on `entitlements/current`, monotonic daily `aiUsage`, immutable `uid`/`createdAt`, strict `affectedKeys().hasOnly()` updates, and zero warnings from `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`), plus a `storage.rules` blueprint ready for optional Stage 1 Cloud Storage.\n- **Expo-Portable Pure Core**: Built framework-independent TypeScript modules with automated unit tests: integer minor-unit currency engine (`IQD` / `USD` / `EUR`), opt-in AES-256-GCM E2E encryption + 24-character Recovery Key generator, entitlements & daily quota evaluator, shared Zod schemas, and the AI Privacy Gate + prompt-injection delimiter wrapper.\n- **Provider-Agnostic AI Engine & Privacy Gate**: Implemented a server-side Express `/api/ai/complete` proxy using `@google/genai` (`gemini-4-hydrogen` primary with `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` fallback, model names driven by config, zero API key in client bundle, response caching, retry backoff, and metadata-only logging). Enforces the **Privacy Gate** on both client and server while `free_tier = true` (blocking Vault files, images, passports/IDs, and locked/E2E notes) and requires an interactive confirmation preview before any mutating action.\n- **Responsive Design System, Tri-Lingual RTL & PWA**: Implemented the Calm Slate & Emerald theme across **Light**, **Dark**, and **AMOLED Black**, full runtime switching and logical RTL mirroring for **English (`en`)**, **Arabic (`ar`)**, and **Kurdish Sorani (`ckb`)**, local PIN App Lock, workspace JSON export, GitHub Actions CI workflow, and installable PWA support (`vite-plugin-pwa`, standalone manifest, standard/maskable/iOS PNG icons, offline banner, and in-app install prompt).\n\n#### How to Test & Verification Results\n- **Unit & Security Invariant Tests**: `npm test && npx tsx --test firestore.rules.test.ts` \342\200\224 **15 / 15 passed** (currency minor-unit math, Privacy Gate free-tier blocks, AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt round-trip, entitlements/quotas, and Firestore rules invariants).\n- **Rules Audit & Typecheck / Build**: `npm run lint:rules` (0 errors), `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit` clean), and `npm run build` (clean production + PWA service worker bundle).\n- **Live Browser Verification**: Verified at desktop (`1440\303\227900`) and mobile (`390\303\227844`) with 0 console errors: theme transitions (Light / Dark / AMOLED), Arabic & Kurdish Sorani RTL mirroring, PIN lock setup, live in-browser AES-256-GCM Recovery Key + round-trip verification, Privacy Gate blocking `\"Scan my passport photo\"`, and mobile zero-overflow (`390 <= 390`) layout. Fixed mobile KPI divider styling, missing Arabic/Kurdish Settings helper strings, and toast auto-dismiss during visual critique and re-verified cleanly.\n- **Manual Check Recommended**: Click **Sign in with Google** in the sidebar to verify live interactive OAuth sign-in and Firestore profile sync (interactive Google OAuth popups cannot be completed automatically by headless verification).\n\n#### Known Limitations & Honest Notes\n- **Web/PWA vs. Native Mobile**: This workspace runs as an installable React Web/PWA. While the pure domain engines, Zod schemas, crypto helpers, and repository contracts are Expo-portable, native mobile features (Face ID/Fingerprint biometrics, native camera edge scanning, Android notification channels, and iOS background scheduling) require an Expo EAS Development Build on your local machine.\n- **Local-Only Vault (Spark Tier)**: Cloud Storage for Firebase requires the Blaze plan, so Vault storage runs in Local-Only mode during Stage 0 to keep billing strictly at $0.\n- **iOS Safari PWA Notifications**: iOS Safari PWAs run offline smoothly, but local scheduled notifications and silent background rescheduling remain limited compared to native iOS builds.\n\n#### Security Considerations\n- Please review and test `firestore.rules` against the Firebase Emulator Suite before opening LifeOS beyond personal Stage 0 use\342\200\224security rules are a living boundary and should be audited whenever new fields or collections are introduced.\n- Keep your generated opt-in E2E **Recovery Key** offline; because LifeOS never stores your passphrase or raw key, lost keys cannot be recovered.\n- While `free_tier = true`, the Privacy Gate intentionally blocks Vault images, passports/IDs, and locked notes from reaching cloud AI.\n\n#### Next Step\nReply **\"Proceed to Phase 2\"** (or share any Phase 1 adjustments) to begin **Phase 2: Debts Manager (+ AI)** \342\200\224 multi-currency IQD/USD/EUR ledgers, idempotent partial payments, deterministic repayment probability, snowball vs. avalanche payoff planner, cash-flow forecast, and multilingual EN/AR/KU polite reminder drafting."
    thinking: "**Observing The Detail**\n\nI\'m currently fixated on a particular mobile screenshot. The image, specifically the `.playwright-cli/r2-mobile-home.png` file, is remarkably clean. The crisp, single-pixel hairline dividers between the KPI cells are perfect. I\'m also impressed by the lack of horizontal overflow and the compact top bar.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "uJ4Ea_LbNIS4sOIPwrrmoQE"
    modified_response: "### Phase 1 Complete \342\200\224 LifeOS Foundation\n\n#### What Was Built\n- **Firebase & Offline-First Sync**: Provisioned Firebase Auth (Google Sign-In; Apple Sign-In isolated behind `auth.apple.enabled = false`) and Cloud Firestore with multi-tab IndexedDB persistent local cache, startup connectivity validation, and structured permission error handling behind a platform-agnostic repository layer (`AuthRepository`, `UserProfileRepository`, `AiUsageRepository`, `LocalVaultStorageAdapter`).\n- **Hardened Security Rules & Blueprint**: Authored the JSON Schema data blueprint, security test specification, composite indexes, and deployed Eight-Pillar `firestore.rules` (strict per-user tenant isolation under `users/{uid}/...`, `email_verified` enforcement, server-only lock on `entitlements/current`, monotonic daily `aiUsage`, immutable `uid`/`createdAt`, strict `affectedKeys().hasOnly()` updates, and zero warnings from `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`), plus a `storage.rules` blueprint ready for optional Stage 1 Cloud Storage.\n- **Expo-Portable Pure Core**: Built framework-independent TypeScript modules with automated unit tests: integer minor-unit currency engine (`IQD` / `USD` / `EUR`), opt-in AES-256-GCM E2E encryption + 24-character Recovery Key generator, entitlements & daily quota evaluator, shared Zod schemas, and the AI Privacy Gate + prompt-injection delimiter wrapper.\n- **Provider-Agnostic AI Engine & Privacy Gate**: Implemented a server-side Express `/api/ai/complete` proxy using `@google/genai` (`gemini-4-hydrogen` primary with `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` fallback, model names driven by config, zero API key in client bundle, response caching, retry backoff, and metadata-only logging). Enforces the **Privacy Gate** on both client and server while `free_tier = true` (blocking Vault files, images, passports/IDs, and locked/E2E notes) and requires an interactive confirmation preview before any mutating action.\n- **Responsive Design