  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Identifying the Error**\n\nOkay, I\'ve zeroed in on the error! I am looking at `/server.ts` particularly lines 242-247, where I am observing the `createViteServer` instantiation. The key is in understanding how `middlewareMode: true` works. I will keep digging to see if there is any other contributing code.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Cause**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough. I understand now that the root of the problem lies in the interaction between Vite\'s `@vite/client` and the `middlewareMode: true` configuration within `server.ts`. It seems that, even with middleware mode enabled, Vite attempts to open a WebSocket connection unless HMR is explicitly disabled, which is what `DISABLE_HMR` is for. I\'m focusing on why this HMR WebSocket connection is failing in the Cloud Run proxy environment. I will be checking both `server.ts` and `vite.config.ts`, and checking the environment_constraints. I need to be sure!\n\n\n"
