  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Product**: **LifeOS** \342\200\224 an offline-first, privacy-hardened, AI-assisted personal life manager (debts, smart reminders, to-do/planner, notes, document vault, habits, finance, global AI assistant) built in phases (Phase 1 through Phase 7, pausing for user approval after each phase).\n- **Resolved User Decisions (from Phase 1 Clarifying Q&A)**:\n  1. **Runtime**: Live React Web/PWA in this AI Studio workspace with an **Expo-portable core** (pure domain logic, Zod schemas, crypto, i18n, and repository interfaces isolated from DOM/Firebase).\n  2. **Storage & Billing**: **Firebase Spark free tier** with **Local-Only Document Vault** first (no Blaze billing required).\n  3. **Localization & Currency**: **English UI** default with **IQD and USD** dual-currency support, plus runtime switching and logical RTL layout for **Arabic (`ar`)** and **Kurdish Sorani (`ckb`)**.\n  4. **E2E Encryption**: **Opt-in per folder/note** client-side AES-256-GCM encryption with user-held Recovery Key.\n  5. **Visual Theme**: **Calm Slate & Emerald** Material You + iOS polish across **Light, Dark, and pure-black AMOLED** themes.\n- **Current Immediate Request**: The user triggered a manual fix for a Vite dev-server HMR WebSocket error appearing in the browser preview:\n  - `error 0: [vite] createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport/connect/</<@https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app/@vite/client:234:30`\n  - `error 1: createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport/connect/</<@https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app/@vite/client:234:30`\n- **Firebase Resource Identifiers**:\n  - Provisioned Firebase Project ID: `excellent-engine-48f9p`\n  - Provisioned Firestore Database ID: `ai-studio-38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872`\n  - Config file: `/firebase-applet-config.json` (auto-created by `ProvisionFirebase` RPC)\n  - Dev App URL: `https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app`\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed (Phase 1 Foundation)\n- **Step 1 Architecture & Plan**: Delivered full Step 1 architecture, Mermaid diagrams, data model, indexes, security rules design, STRIDE-lite threat model, cost model, and roadmap; user answered 5 clarifying questions and approved `/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872/implementation_plan.md`.\n- **Firebase Provisioning & Deployed Rules**:\n  - Verified ToS (`fax.GetFirebaseTos` -> `{\"accepted\": true}`) and provisioned Firebase (`fax.ProvisionFirebase`, `platform: \"web\"`).\n  - Created `/firebase-blueprint.json`, `/security_spec.md`, `/firestore.rules`, `/storage.rules`, `/firestore.indexes.json`, `/firestore.rules.test.ts`, `/eslint.config.mjs`.\n  - Audited `/firestore.rules` with `npx eslint firestore.rules` (0 errors/warnings) and deployed via `fax.DeployRules` (succeeded).\n- **Packages Installed**: `firebase`, `zustand`, `zod`, `i18next`, `react-i18next`, `vite-plugin-pwa`, `@google/genai@latest`, `eslint`, `@firebase/eslint-plugin-security-rules`.\n- **Configuration & PWA Assets**:\n  - Updated `/metadata.json` (`name: \"LifeOS\"`, `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API`), `/index.html` (fonts `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `DM Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`, `IBM Plex Sans Arabic`, PWA/iOS meta, zero-flash theme/RTL script), `/package.json` (`dev: \"tsx server.ts\"`, `start: \"node server.ts\"`, `lint:rules`, `test`), `/tsconfig.json` (`vite-plugin-pwa/client`), `/vite.config.ts` (`VitePWA` with `maximumFileSizeToCacheInBytes: 5 * 1024 * 1024`), `/.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n  - Generated `/public/icon.svg`, `/public/pwa-192x192.png`, `/public/pwa-512x512.png`, `/public/pwa-maskable-512x512.png`, `/public/apple-touch-icon.png`.\n- **Backend Server**: Created `/server.ts` (Express + Vite middleware in dev, `/api/ai/config`, `/api/ai/complete` using `@google/genai` with `gemini-4-hydrogen` primary + `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` fallback, server-side Privacy Gate, Zod output validation, rate limit, metadata-only logging).\n- **Expo-Portable Pure Core + Unit Tests (all 15/15 passing)**:\n  - `/src/core/currency/currency.ts` + `.test.ts` (integer minor-unit math, FX conversion, EN/AR/CKB formatting)\n  - `/src/core/ai/privacyGate.ts` + `.test.ts` (free-tier sensitive payload blocking, untrusted input wrapping, deterministic cache keys)\n  - `/src/core/ai/llmProvider.ts` (provider-agnostic `LLMProvider` + `ServerProxyLLMProvider`)\n  - `/src/core/crypto/e2eCrypto.ts` + `.test.ts` (WebCrypto PBKDF2-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM + 24-char Recovery Key)\n  - `/src/core/entitlements/entitlements.ts` + `.test.ts` (Free/Pro/Family catalog, Stage 0 feature flags, daily quota evaluator)\n  - `/src/core/schemas/userProfileSchema.ts` (Zod schemas synchronized with `firebase-blueprint.json`)\n  - `/src/core/i18n/i18n.ts` (EN / AR / CKB translations + `document.documentElement.dir` sync)\n- **Data Layer & UI**:\n  - `/src/data/firebase/firebaseClient.ts` (Firebase JS SDK, Firestore `persistentLocalCache` + `persistentMultipleTabManager`, startup `testFirestoreConnection()`, structured `handleFirestoreError`)\n  - `/src/data/repositories/interfaces.ts` & `/src/data/repositories/firebaseWebAdapter.ts`\n  - `/src/state/useUIStore.ts` (Zustand UI state, theme/RTL, PIN lock, local offline cache)\n  - `/src/hooks/useLifeOS.ts` (`usePWAInstall`, `useOnlineStatus`, `useLifeOSSync`, `persistProfilePatch`)\n  - `/src/components/`: `ErrorBoundary.tsx`, `PWAInstallButton.tsx`, `AppLockOverlay.tsx`, `AICommandPalette.tsx`, `AppShell.tsx`\n  - `/src/features/`: `home/ui/HomeView.tsx`, `settings/ui/SettingsView.tsx`, `modules/ui/ModuleReadinessView.tsx`\n  - `/src/App.tsx`, `/src/main.tsx`, `/src/index.css`\n- **Verification Completed for Phase 1**:\n  - Unit tests + rules test (`15/15` passed), `npx eslint firestore.rules` (0 errors), `compile_applet` (succeeded), `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit` succeeded).\n  - Live `playwright-cli` browser verification completed at desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`): Light/Dark/AMOLED themes, Arabic/Kurdish RTL mirroring, PIN Lock, AES-256-GCM Recovery Key + round-trip verification, Privacy Gate blocking `\"Scan my passport photo\"`, zero horizontal overflow (`390 <= 390`).\n\n### Skills Read\n- `/skills/system_skills/planning_mode/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` + `references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md` + `references/error-handling-and-sdk.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` + `references/3_saas_dashboard.md` + `references/10_mobile_touch_apps.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/pwa_integration/SKILL.md`\n\n### In Progress\n- Investigating and fixing the Vite HMR WebSocket error reported by the user (`createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport/connect` in `/@vite/client`).\n- Diagnostic run just completed: `curl -s http://localhost:3000/` showed `<script type=\"module\" src=\"/@vite/client\"></script>` is being injected, and `DISABLE_HMR` is NOT set (`DISABLE_HMR=` empty) in the shell environment (or when `server.ts` runs `createViteServer({ server: { middlewareMode: true }, appType: \'spa\' })`).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Root Cause of Current WebSocket Error**:\n  - In `/server.ts` lines 242\342\200\223247:\n    ```ts\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\n      appType: \'spa\',\n    });\n    ```\n  - When Vite 8 runs in `middlewareMode: true` inside an Express server without passing `hmr: false` (or without attaching an HTTP server to `server.hmr.server`), Vite starts a separate standalone HMR WebSocket server on port `24678` (or tries to connect `@vite/client` via `wss://ais-dev-.../` which cannot upgrade through the Express middleware when no `httpServer` is bound, and AI Studio explicitly disables HMR in this preview environment).\n  - Furthermore, in `vite.config.ts`, `hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\'` evaluates to `true` whenever `DISABLE_HMR` is unset (and in `server.ts`, `server: { middlewareMode: true }` did not explicitly disable HMR or attach an `http.Server`).\n  - **Clean Fix**:\n    1. In `/server.ts`, pass `hmr: false` (or `hmr: process.env.ENABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? { server: httpServer } : false`\342\200\224since AI Studio environment constraints explicitly specify `HMR: Disabled`, setting `hmr: false` in `createViteServer({ server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false, watch: null }, appType: \'spa\' })` when `DISABLE_HMR === \'true\'` OR unconditionally `hmr: false` in AI Studio/middleware mode cleanly stops `@vite/client` from attempting any failing WebSocket connection!).\n    2. Wait: verify whether Vite 8\'s `@vite/client` still attempts a WebSocket connection when `server.hmr = false`! Check `vite.config.ts` and test with `curl -s http://localhost:3000/@vite/client` and `playwright-cli` console errors AND check if `createServer` with `http.createServer(app)` + `hmr: false` eliminates `createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport` completely!\n    - Also double-check `vite-plugin-pwa`\'s `devOptions.enabled: true` doesn\'t inject anything conflicting, and check `vite.config.ts` comment:\n      `// HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.`\n      Note: Keep `vite.config.ts`\'s `DISABLE_HMR` check intact (do not break the template contract), and in `/server.ts` pass `hmr: false` inside `createViteServer({ server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false }, appType: \'spa\' })` (or check why `DISABLE_HMR` wasn\'t passed to `tsx server.ts` \342\200\224 wait: in `server.ts` `middlewareMode: true`, attaching `httpServer` vs setting `hmr: false`: setting `hmr: false` in `server.ts` guarantees zero WebSocket connection errors from `@vite/client` in Cloud Run / AI Studio iframe!).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **[Resolved] Workbox precache size error during `compile_applet`**:\n   - Error: `Assets exceeding the limit: assets/index-*.js is 2.51 MB` (default Workbox cap is 2 MiB on unminified `--minify false` builds).\n   - Fix: Added `maximumFileSizeToCacheInBytes: 5 * 1024 * 1024` in `vite.config.ts` under `VitePWA -> workbox`. Verified `compile_applet` succeeded.\n2. **[Resolved] Round 1 Visual Critique Defects**:\n   - Mobile KPI strip had dark default `divide-y` lines -> switched to `gap-px` on `HomeView.tsx`.\n   - SettingsView had 6 untranslated English helper strings in AR/CKB -> added translation keys in `src/core/i18n/i18n.ts` and bound them in `SettingsView.tsx`.\n   - Toast stayed pinned indefinitely -> added auto-dismiss timer + scroll-to-top on route change in `AppShell.tsx`.\n   - Re-verified cleanly in Round 2.\n3. **[Unresolved \342\200\224 Active Task] Vite WebSocket HMR Connection Error in Preview**:\n   - Error: `[vite] createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport/connect/</<@https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app/@vite/client:234:30`\n   - Cause: `/server.ts` creates Vite in `middlewareMode: true` without disabling `hmr` (and without binding an HTTP server to HMR), so `@vite/client` attempts a `wss://` WebSocket upgrade that fails on the proxied Cloud Run preview URL.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server runs via `npm run dev` (`tsx server.ts`) on port `3000`.\n- `playwright-cli` and headless Chromium are pre-installed and working cleanly in `/app/applet`.\n- Note: Do NOT touch Firebase config or re-provision Firebase unless needed; `firebase-applet-config.json` and deployed `firestore.rules` are already live and healthy.\n- Remember: Because the additional metadata reminds us to load the Firebase skill when interacting with Firestore/Firebase services, only load it if modifying Firebase/Firestore code (this bug is purely in Vite middleware HMR config in `server.ts`).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Fix Vite HMR WebSocket error in `/server.ts`**:\n   - Inspect lines 230\342\200\223265 of `/server.ts`.\n   - Update `createViteServer` options to disable HMR cleanly in middleware mode (`server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false, watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : undefined }` \342\200\224 or verify whether Vite 8 needs `ws: false` as well as `hmr: false`!).\n   - Important: Check Vite 8\'s `@vite/client` response (`curl -s http://localhost:3000/@vite/client | grep -n \"createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport\\|ws\"`) after restarting the dev server to confirm `server.ws: false` / `server.hmr: false` prevents `@vite/client` from attempting any WebSocket connection at all!\n   - If Vite 8 still attempts a WebSocket connection unless `ws: false` is set in `server` config, pass `server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false, ws: false }` (verify TypeScript types via `lint_applet`).\n2. **Verify Fix End-to-End**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in parallel.\n   - Call `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Verify with `playwright-cli`: open `http://localhost:3000`, wait 1\342\200\2232s, inspect `playwright-cli console` (all messages, errors & warnings) and `playwright-cli network` (or evaluate WebSocket errors) to confirm zero `[vite]` WebSocket errors and healthy page render, then `playwright-cli close`.\n   - Confirm `npm test` still passes if any shared code was touched (unlikely if only `server.ts` changed).\n3. **Respond Concisely to the User**:\n   - Explain the root cause (Vite middleware HMR WebSocket connection in `server.ts`) and the fix applied, confirm zero console/WebSocket errors, and invite the user to say **\"Proceed to Phase 2\"** when ready for the Debts Manager module.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Phased Execution Contract**: Do NOT start Phase 2 (Debts Manager) until the user explicitly approves moving to Phase 2. Right now, only fix the reported Vite WebSocket error cleanly.\n- **No Unnecessary Rewrites**: Make surgical edits only to `/server.ts` (and `/vite.config.ts` only if strictly required for `ws: false`).\n- **Build/Lint Verification**: Always co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` on the final build check before finishing the turn, and restart the dev server (`restart_dev_server`) before browser verification.\n- **Honest Reporting**: Only claim what was actually tested and observed after the last edit.\n</summary>"
