  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Vite\'s Actions**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! By digging into Vite 8\'s source, I\'ve confirmed that `devHtmlHook` consistently injects `<script type=\"module\" src=\"/@`. Secondly, Vite 8 *always* wraps the HTML body in a `<div id=\"root\">`, even when explicitly configured to not do so. These details are vital.\n\n\n**Analyzing HMR Mechanism**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Vite\'s Hot Module Replacement (HMR) implementation, specifically focusing on `client.mjs`. I\'ve observed that this file establishes a WebSocket connection using a token, targeting a port that, crucially, is not exposed on Cloud Run. This causes an immediate WebSocket error. I also need to verify what happens in `client.mjs` when `server.hmr = false` and `server.ws = false`.\n\n\n"
