  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing WebSocket Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how Vite configures WebSocket connections, specifically examining the `index.d.ts` file within the `vite` module. Line 2306 highlights the `ws` option, and I am parsing through the comments and types to clarify its role in enabling/disabling the WebSocket server.\n\n\n**Clarifying WebSocket Logic**\n\nI\'m now digging deeper into how Vite handles `ws: false` versus `ws: { server: httpServer }`. It seems even with `ws: false`, `devHtmlHook` *still* injects `/@vite/client`, which initially appeared counterintuitive. However, with `ws: false`, `createWebSocketServer` returns a no-op stub. Consequently, `@vite/client` would fail to connect. Conversely, `ws: { server: httpServer }` utilizes the existing HTTP server and allows for specific hostnames with `allowedHosts: true`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "CKEEa8eKFLfqvdIPy5uc8AI"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6888541142134250711"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Attach Express http.Server to Vite middleware WebSocket server with allowedHosts enabled so @vite/client connects on port 3000/443 instead of failing on unexposed port 24678.\", \"Instruction\":\"Import Node\'s http module, create an httpServer wrapping Express, pass ws: { server: httpServer } and allowedHosts: true to createViteServer in dev mode, and listen via httpServer.listen.\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":5, \"ReplacementContent\":\"import \'dotenv/config\';\\nimport express from \'express\';\\nimport http from \'http\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\", \"StartLine\":1, \"TargetContent\":\"import \'dotenv/config\';\\nimport express from \'express\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":302, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const httpServer = http.createServer(app);\\n\\n  if (!IS_PROD) {\\n    const { createServer: createViteServer } = await import(\'vite\');\\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: {\\n        middlewareMode: true,\\n        allowedHosts: true,\\n        ws: { server: httpServer },\\n        hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\\n      },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  } else {\\n    const distPath = path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\');\\n    app.use(express.static(distPath));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (_req, res) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.join(distPath, \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  httpServer.listen(PORT, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n    console.log(`LifeOS server listening on http://0.0.0.0:${PORT}`);\\n  });\\n}\", \"StartLine\":282, \"TargetContent\":\"  if (!IS_PROD) {\\n    const { createServer: createViteServer } = await import(\'vite\');\\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  } else {\\n    const distPath = path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\');\\n    app.use(express.static(distPath));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (_req, res) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.join(distPath, \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  app.listen(PORT, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n    console.log(`LifeOS server listening on http://0.0.0.0:${PORT}`);\\n  });\\n}\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating Vite middleware WebSocket binding in server.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix Vite WS binding in server.ts\"}"
