  planner_response {
    response: "Fixed the Vite WebSocket connection error in the development server:\n\n- **Cause:** Vite middleware mode defaulted to advertising HMR WebSocket port `24678` (`hmrPort = 24678`) without an attached HTTP server or host allowlist, causing `/@vite/client` to fail connecting through the single-port preview proxy.\n- **Fix:** Bound Vite\'s WebSocket upgrade handler directly to the Express `http.Server` on port `3000` with `allowedHosts: true` and `DISABLE_HMR` respected, so client connections route over the same origin and port (`hmrPort = null`).\n- **Verification:** Rebuilt (`compile_applet`), type-checked (`lint_applet`), restarted the dev server, and confirmed in a headless browser check that the page renders with **0 console errors and 0 warnings**.\n\nWhen you\'re ready to build the Debts Manager module, reply **\"Proceed to Phase 2\"**."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Verification Metrics**\n\nOkay, I\'m thrilled! I\'ve just verified that I\'m no longer dealing with a phantom port, which is fantastic news. Also, I\'m now certain that I have absolutely zero console errors, WebSocket errors, or even warnings. Total triumph! I\'m now focused on the next verification point.\n\n\n"
