  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Phase 2 Debts**\n\nI\'m now carefully designing Phase 2, focusing on principal-architect precision. I\'m reviewing the approved architecture and vision documents to pinpoint every required capability, starting with data models and Firestore security rules. My aim is to build a robust and secure foundation for the debts manager.\n\n\n**Addressing Data Schema Gaps**\n\nI\'m expanding the data model with `DebtRecord`, `DebtLedger`, and a `DebtPayment` subcollection. The new `DebtRecord` schema will have fields like `uid`, `direction`, `personKey`, `principalMinor`, `remainingMinor`, `interestRateBps`, and `dueDate`. I\'m paying close attention to data integrity, especially in terminal state locks to prevent updates when settled.\n\n\n**Defining Payment History**\n\nI\'ve specified the `DebtPayment` subcollection fields, including `uid`, `debtId`, `amountMinor`, currency details, and payment method options, as well as timestamps. I am also planning the immutable ledger entries, focusing on validations to ensure data integrity.\n\n\n**Adding User Metadata**\n\nI am now enriching the `UserProfile` data. I\'m adding `personPhone` (optional), `onTimeCount`, `lateCount`, `activeDebtCount`, `version`, `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`. I must update `firebase-blueprint.json` with the new data model. I need to also ensure all Firestore security rules are updated. The test suite requires attention for this update too. I am going to make this offline-first, like the `UserProfile`.\n\n\n**Implementing Debt Core Logic**\n\nI\'m now building the core debt engine within `/src/core/debts/`. I\'ve defined `debtSchemas.ts` with Zod schemas that mirror `firebase-blueprint.json` including the `normalizePersonKey(name)` helper. This converts names into deterministic keys. I am developing `debtEngine.ts`, focusing on multi-currency aggregation and net positions, to compute exact integer totals for each currency.\n\n\n**Developing Debt Score Logic**\n\nI am now implementing a deterministic repayment probability score. I am focusing on a transparent Bayesian/weighted formula, incorporating counterparty payment history and debt progress. I\'m building it to return a score, band, and a list of factors explaining the logic. I am also planning to include a Snowball vs. Avalanche payoff planner. I will also incorporate an explicit, user-editable FX rate snapshot, ensuring it\'s clearly labeled as an estimate.\n\n\n**Planning Payoff Simulations**\n\nI\'m now incorporating payoff simulations. I\'m focusing on user-defined monthly budgets and payoff strategies (snowball vs. avalanche). The simulation will provide deterministic amortization for up to 120 months in minor units. I\'m aiming to compute the payoff order, projected payoff month per debt, the total time to debt freedom, and interest savings compared to a minimum payment approach.\n\n**Constructing Cash-Flow Forecast**\n\nI am now building the 30/60/90-day cash flow forecast. I will deterministically bucket upcoming due dates into overdue, next 30 days, 31-60 days, 61-90 days, beyond 90 days, and no due date. The forecast will show expected inflows (owed to me), outflows (I owe), and the net cash impact per currency.\n\n**Defining Payment Helpers**\n\nI am now creating settlement and payment math helpers. I will validate `amountMinor` (must be greater than zero and less than or equal to remaining balance) and calculate the next remaining balance, status (settled or partial), and a determination of on-time payment based on due date.\n\n**Implementing CSV Export**\n\nI am now implementing a CSV export function. I will focus on exporting relevant debt data in a structured CSV format.\n\n\n**Verifying System Integrations**\n\nI\'ve crafted a CSV serializer with formula injection neutralization and robust test suites using `node:test` in `/src/core/debts/debtEngine.test.ts`. These tests ensure data integrity for multi-currency net balance, settlement math, repayment probability, cash-flow forecast, and CSV protection. I am confident that these are ready for use.\n\n\n**Refining UI Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the user interface integration. I\'ve built a **Draft Debt Proposal** that takes inputs (e.g., Arabic debts), returns a validated draft, and opens a Confirmation Preview form. I also developed a POST endpoint to craft reminders. I will be updating the HomeView and integrating real-time debts totals into the daily briefing.\n\n\n**Integrating Debts UI**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating the Debt feature within the `AppShell` and activating it on the HomeView. I\'m moving forward with a calm slate and emerald design, supporting EN/AR/CKB RTL on desktop and mobile. I am working on a UI with single-elevation flat surfaces with hairline borders and logical CSS for RTL mirroring. I\'m building a Tab Bar with four sub-views for debt ledger, debt proposal, payoff planner, and cash-flow forecast.\n\n\n**Designing UI Debt List**\n\nI\'m now designing the debt list user interface elements. I am crafting a feature-rich, high-density list with filters (language parser with Confirmation Preview), live search input, direction filters, status filters, and CSV export. I\'m focusing on clean debt list rows displaying counterparty, direction, progress, and quick actions. The UI will support EN/AR/CKB RTL on both desktop and mobile.\n\n\n**Building Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now building the interactive modal for debt management. I am developing an \"Add/Edit Debt\" modal, a \"Log Payment/Settle\" modal, and a \"Debt Detail & Payment History\" drawer. These modals will include accessible designs and zero-flicker behavior. I am also working on an AI-powered reminder message drafter modal, enabling language and tone customization.\n\n\n\n"
    message_id: "uKMEa9e7GPjP-8YPooTT6Aw"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_12958913296371615090"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Enrich DebtLedger and DebtRecord schemas and add DebtPayment entity and subcollection path in firebase-blueprint.json for Phase 2 Debts Manager.\", \"EndLine\":111, \"Instruction\":\"Update DebtLedger and DebtRecord entity definitions and add DebtPayment entity definition.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"    \\\"DebtLedger\\\": {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"DebtLedger\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Denormalized per-person multi-currency ledger totals and repayment reliability.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"uid\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 128, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\" },\\n        \\\"personName\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 120 },\\n        \\\"personPhone\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 32 },\\n        \\\"onTimeCount\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"lateCount\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"activeDebtCount\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"version\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"format\\\": \\\"date-time\\\" },\\n        \\\"updatedAt\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"format\\\": \\\"date-time\\\" }\\n      },\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"uid\\\", \\\"personName\\\", \\\"onTimeCount\\\", \\\"lateCount\\\", \\\"activeDebtCount\\\", \\\"version\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\", \\\"updatedAt\\\"]\\n    },\\n    \\\"DebtRecord\\\": {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"DebtRecord\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Individual debt record stored strictly in integer minor units with integer APR basis points.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"uid\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 128, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\" },\\n        \\\"direction\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"i_owe\\\", \\\"owed_to_me\\\"] },\\n        \\\"personKey\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 128, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\" },\\n        \\\"personName\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 120 },\\n        \\\"personPhone\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 32 },\\n        \\\"category\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"personal\\\", \\\"family\\\", \\\"business\\\", \\\"loan\\\", \\\"bill_split\\\", \\\"other\\\"] },\\n        \\\"principalMinor\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"remainingMinor\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"currency\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"IQD\\\", \\\"USD\\\", \\\"EUR\\\"] },\\n        \\\"interestRateBps\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"dueDate\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 10, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^\\\\\\\\d{4}-\\\\\\\\d{2}-\\\\\\\\d{2}$\\\" },\\n        \\\"status\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"active\\\", \\\"partial\\\", \\\"overdue\\\", \\\"settled\\\"] },\\n        \\\"notes\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 2000 },\\n        \\\"paymentCount\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"lastPaymentDate\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 10, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^\\\\\\\\d{4}-\\\\\\\\d{2}-\\\\\\\\d{2}$\\\" },\\n        \\\"version\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"format\\\": \\\"date-time\\\" },\\n        \\\"updatedAt\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"format\\\": \\\"date-time\\\" }\\n      },\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\n        \\\"uid\\\",\\n        \\\"direction\\\",\\n        \\\"personKey\\\",\\n        \\\"personName\\\",\\n        \\\"category\\\",\\n        \\\"principalMinor\\\",\\n        \\\"remainingMinor\\\",\\n        \\\"currency\\\",\\n        \\\"interestRateBps\\\",\\n        \\\"status\\\",\\n        \\\"paymentCount\\\",\\n        \\\"version\\\",\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\",\\n        \\\"updatedAt\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \\\"DebtPayment\\\": {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"DebtPayment\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Immutable append-only repayment ledger entry under a specific debt.\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"uid\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 128, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\" },\\n        \\\"debtId\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 1, \\\"maxLength\\\": 128, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\\\" },\\n        \\\"amountMinor\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"currency\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"IQD\\\", \\\"USD\\\", \\\"EUR\\\"] },\\n        \\\"paidOn\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 10, \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^\\\\\\\\d{4}-\\\\\\\\d{2}-\\\\\\\\d{2}$\\\" },\\n        \\\"method\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"cash\\\", \\\"bank_transfer\\\", \\\"zaincash\\\", \\\"fib\\\", \\\"fastpay\\\", \\\"other\\\"] },\\n        \\\"note\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"maxLength\\\": 500 },\\n        \\\"wasOnTime\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\" },\\n        \\\"createdAt\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"format\\\": \\\"date-time\\\" }\\n      },\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"uid\\\", \\\"debtId\\\", \\\"amountMinor\\\", \\\"currency\\\", \\\"paidOn\\\", \\\"method\\\", \\\"wasOnTime\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\"]\\n    },\", \"StartLine\":75, \"TargetContent\":\"    \\\"DebtLedger\\\": {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"DebtLedger\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\