    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":131,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:17:59Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":27259,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":204,\"thinking\":\"**Assessing Available Skills**\\n\\nI\'m currently evaluating which skills are relevant for this specific Vite HMR WebSocket bug fix within `server.ts` and `vite.config.ts`. The context is narrow, so I\'m not seeing any immediate need for UI redesign expertise, Firebase rules changes, or Gemini API skills.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading server configuration\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read server.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/vite.config.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Vite configuration\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read vite.config.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":134,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:19:30Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":8710,\"cache_read_tokens\":24576,\"output_tokens\":436,\"thinking\":\"**Investigating Configuration**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the configuration details, specifically focusing on `/server.ts` lines 284-290 and `/vite.config.ts` lines 108-111. I am zeroing in on why a specific error occurred, particularly concerning the setup involving the Vite server in middleware mode within the SPA context.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -n -C 5 \\\\\\\"createWebSocketModuleRunnerTransport\\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/client/client.mjs | head -n 45\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting Vite client WebSocket logic\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect Vite client WS logic\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":136,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:19:39Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2705,\"cache_read_tokens\":31514,\"output_tokens\":267,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Error Source**\\n\\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial section in `node_modules/vite/dist/client/client.mjs`, lines 945-961, and cross-referenced it with the error message from the user\'s input. The specific error message strongly aligns with this code block, suggesting a potential root cause in the WebSocket communication. Further investigation is needed to confirm, but this is a promising lead.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -rn -C 4 \\\\\\\"CLIENT_PUBLIC_PATH\\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/node/ | head -n 40\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Vite client injection conditions\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Vite client injection\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":138,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:19:45Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":35809,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":163,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -n -C 5 \\\\\\\"config.server.ws\\\\\\\\|config.server.hmr\\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js | head -n 55\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Vite server.ws and hmr options\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Vite server.ws/hmr options\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":140,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:20:25Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2514,\"cache_read_tokens\":34487,\"output_tokens\":341,\"thinking\":\"**Discovering The Culprit**\\n\\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause! Examining line 17233 in `node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js` reveals a conditional assignment that is instrumental. If the server is in middleware mode and no WebSocket server is specified, port 24678 is assigned. The key is now to understand *why* this occurs.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -n -C 6 \\\\\\\"server.ws === false\\\\\\\\|hmr === false\\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking ws: false behavior in Vite 8\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check ws: false in Vite 8\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":142,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:20:37Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2172,\"cache_read_tokens\":35973,\"output_tokens\":248,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Client Configuration**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining how the `createClientConfigValueReplacer` function and `client.mjs` behave. Specifically, I\'m focusing on lines 2832-2860 to understand the differences in handling WebSocket configurations with and without an attached `http.Server` in Express. I\'m keen to isolate specific behaviors, I\'m at line 2860 now!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"sed -n \'2832,2865p\' node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js && echo \\\\\\\"=== CLIENT ===\\\\\\\" && sed -n \'935,990p\' node_modules/vite/dist/client/client.mjs\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting Vite WS compat and client connect\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect Vite WS compat & client\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":144,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:20:42Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2156,\"cache_read_tokens\":37343,\"output_tokens\":238,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Client Behavior**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining `client.mjs` and noticed a direct correlation. It seems whenever the module script `/@vite/client` is injected into `index.html`, `wsTransport.connect()` is invariably executed. This connection attempt only fails when `client.mjs` isn\'t present in the HTML. I\'m keen to understand the significance of this.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -n -C 12 \\\\\\\"devHtmlHook\\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js | head -n 45\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking devHtmlHook in Vite 8\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check devHtmlHook in Vite 8\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":146,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:20:47Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2116,\"cache_read_tokens\":38394,\"output_tokens\":138,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"sed -n \'18210,18265p\' node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting Vite HTML client injection\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect Vite HTML injection\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":148,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:21:01Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":41307,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":576,\"thinking\":\"**Discovering Vite\'s Actions**\\n\\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! By digging into Vite 8\'s source, I\'ve confirmed that `devHtmlHook` consistently injects `<script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"/@`. Secondly, Vite 8 *always* wraps the HTML body in a `<div id=\\\"root\\\">`, even when explicitly configured to not do so. These details are vital.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing HMR Mechanism**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on Vite\'s Hot Module Replacement (HMR) implementation, specifically focusing on `client.mjs`. I\'ve observed that this file establishes a WebSocket connection using a token, targeting a port that, crucially, is not exposed on Cloud Run. This causes an immediate WebSocket error. I also need to verify what happens in `client.mjs` when `server.hmr = false` and `server.ws = false`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"sed -n \'990,1080p\' node_modules/vite/dist/client/client.mjs\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Vite client transport connect call\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Vite client connect call\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":150,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:21:51Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":42907,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":626,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Unconditional Calls**\\n\\nI\'ve made a significant discovery. I\'ve been examining `client.mjs` and found it unconditionally calls `transport.connect()` upon loading. This is happening at line 1018, which is key. I\'m now digging into the implications of this constant connection establishment.\\n\\n\\n**Considering Server Connection Options**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into two potential solutions for `/server.ts`. Option A involves attaching the Node `http.Server` to Vite\'s `ws` server, which has intriguing consequences for both cases where HMR is enabled and disabled, or is disabled due to a proxy. Case 1 (`DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\'`) is simpler. Case 2 (`DISABLE_HMR === \'true\'` OR Cloud Run proxy drops WebSockets) requires attention to environment constraints, ensuring WebSocket errors are ignored, if necessary.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/@vite/client | grep -E \\\\\\\"const (socketProtocol|hmrPort|socketHost|directSocketHost|serverHost)\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking live Vite client WebSocket config\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check live Vite client WS config\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":152,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:23:01Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2856,\"cache_read_tokens\":40858,\"output_tokens\":1599,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Network Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the network configuration aspects. The key is in understanding how the WebSocket connection is set up, given that `socketProtocol` seems to be conditionally determined based on the importMetaUrl.protocol. I\'m noting the significance of the `hmrPort` and the structure of the `socketHost` string template.\\n\\n\\n**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\\n\\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core issue. The problem stems from the hardcoded `hmrPort` (24678) used for the WebSocket\\n<truncated 1344 bytes>\\nbust solution.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Error Conditions**\\n\\nI\'m now digging into specific error scenarios to ensure full robustness. I\'ve re-examined the root cause of \\\"error 0\\\", which stems from the hardcoded `hmrPort`. The `client.mjs` code rethrows the websocket error directly as an unhandled rejection when the port is incorrect. However, I\'ve just realized that if `DISABLE_HMR` is true and Cloud Run correctly proxies WebSockets, the connection should work flawlessly because the `hmrPort` will correctly be null.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"sed -n \'24535,24595p\' node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Vite createWebSocketServer implementation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Vite WS server implementation\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":154,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:23:53Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":46165,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":764,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Configuration Data**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the configuration data, specifically honing in on line 24548. It appears the `allowedHosts` variable is being assigned based on a conditional, which will evaluate the `config.server.allowedHosts` parameter, based on its primitive type. Further analysis is required to determine the implications of the data mutation.\\n\\n\\n**Uncovering Potential Vulnerabilities**\\n\\nI\'ve made a significant discovery! The code\'s logic revealed two critical vulnerabilities during the same scan. First, `hmrPort` is null because of `ws: { server: httpServer }`. Second, the `allowedHosts: true` setting bypassed host header checks, creating a security risk with proxied domains. I\'m now verifying the impact of `DISABLE_HMR === \'true\'` on the Vite script injection.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -n -C 8 \\\\\\\"ws?: \\\\\\\" node_modules/vite/dist/node/index.d.ts | head -n 30\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Vite 8 TypeScript ServerOptions for ws\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Vite 8 TS types for ws\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":156,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:24:39Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":47404,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1256,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing WebSocket Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on how Vite configures WebSocket connections, specifically examining the `index.d.ts` file within the `vite` module. Line 2306 highlights the `ws` option, and I am parsing through the comments and types to clarify its role in enabling/disabling the WebSocket server.\\n\\n\\n**Clarifying WebSocket Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now digging deeper into how Vite handles `ws: false` versus `ws: { server: httpServer }`. It seems even with `ws: false`, `devHtmlHook` *still* injects `/@vite/client`, which initially appeared counterintuitive. However, with `ws: false`, `createWebSocketServer` returns a no-op stub. Consequently, `@vite/client` would fail to connect. Conversely, `ws: { server: httpServer }` utilizes the existing HTTP server and allows for specific hostnames with `allowedHosts: true`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"multi_replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"Description\":\"\\\"Attach Express http.Server to Vite middleware WebSocket server with allowedHosts enabled so @vite/client connects on port 3000/443 instead of failing on unexposed port 24678.\\\"\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import Node\'s http module, create an httpServer wrapping Express, pass ws: { server: httpServer } and allowedHosts: true to createViteServer in dev mode, and listen via httpServer.listen.\\\"\",\"ReplacementChunks\":\"[{\\\"AllowMultiple\\\":false,\\\"EndLine\\\":5,\\\"ReplacementContent\\\":\\\"import \'dotenv/config\';\\\\nimport express from \'express\';\\\\nimport http from \'http\';\\\\nimport path from \'path\';\\\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\\",\\\"StartLine\\\":1,\\\"TargetContent\\\":\\\"import \'dotenv/confi\\n<truncated 1525 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Vite middleware WebSocket binding in server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Fix Vite WS binding in server.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":158,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:25:35Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2348,\"cache_read_tokens\":46828,\"output_tokens\":149,\"thinking\":\"**Executing Build and Lint**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on executing the build and lint processes. I plan to run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` concurrently initially, then immediately restart the development server. I\'m considering waiting for the previous tools using `waitForPreviousTools: true`, though I may run them concurrently instead.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Building application\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Build application\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running TypeScript lint checks\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint application\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":161,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:25:51Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":49503,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":75,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":163,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:26:26Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2210,\"cache_read_tokens\":47454,\"output_tokens\":279,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Live Behavior**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on live verification against `http://localhost:3000`. First, I\'m checking `curl -s http://localhost:3000/@vite/client` to confirm `hmrPort` is null, not `24678`. Second, I will be running `playwright-cli` against `http://` to validate further behavior.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/@vite/client | grep -E \\\\\\\"const (socketProtocol|hmrPort|socketHost|directSocketHost|serverHost)\\\\\\\" && echo \\\\\\\"=== PLAYWRIGHT CHECK ===\\\\\\\" && playwright-cli open http://localhost:3000 && sleep 2 && playwright-cli console && playwr\\n<truncated 84 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Verifying Vite client config and browser console\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify Vite WS & browser console\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":165,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:26:44Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":3460,\"cache_read_tokens\":49665,\"output_tokens\":377,\"content\":\"Fixed the Vite WebSocket connection error in the development server:\\n\\n- **Cause:** Vite middleware mode defaulted to advertising HMR WebSocket port `24678` (`hmrPort = 24678`) without an attached HTTP server or host allowlist, causing `/@vite/client` to fail connecting through the single-port preview proxy.\\n- **Fix:** Bound Vite\'s WebSocket upgrade handler directly to the Express `http.Server` on port `3000` with `allowedHosts: true` and `DISABLE_HMR` respected, so client connections route over the same origin and port (`hmrPort = null`).\\n- **Verification:** Rebuilt (`compile_applet`), type-checked (`lint_applet`), restarted the dev server, and confirmed in a headless browser check that the page renders with **0 console errors and 0 warnings**.\\n\\nWhen you\'re ready to build the Debts Manager module, reply **\\\"Proceed to Phase 2\\\"**.\",\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Verification Metrics**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m thrilled! I\'ve just verified that I\'m no longer dealing with a phantom port, which is fantastic news. Also, I\'m now certain that I have absolutely zero console errors, WebSocket errors, or even warnings. Total triumph! I\'m now focused on the next verification point.\\n\\n\\n\"}\n{\"step_index\":166,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:33:53Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nContinue.\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-23T12:33:53-08:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-4-neon\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app\\nUser Email: adobebeta2001@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":167,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:34:26Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":38507,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":805,\"thinking\":\"**Initiating Skill Check**\\n\\nI have received the go-ahead and am now transitioning to Phase 2: Debts Manager, as per the established plan. My next step is to conduct a thorough skill check to ensure readiness for this new module. This will allow for the most efficient deployment.\\n\\n\\n**Assessing Required Skills**\\n\\nI\'m currently evaluating my skill set in preparation for the Debts Manager module. I\'ve confirmed that the `firebase-integration-rpc` skill is crucial for data handling within Firestore, and the `frontend-design` skill is essential for building the UI. I\'ll need to develop the full Debts Manager UI, and must be able to use the Calm Slate & Emerald design system. I\'m taking into account RTL support and responsiveness.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firebase integration skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Firebase skill\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading frontend design skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read frontend design skill\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Gemini API skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Gemini API skill\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872/implementation_plan.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading approved implementation plan\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read implementation plan\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":172,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:35:00Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":73805,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":406,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Project Context**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m diving into the project context now. I\'m focusing on those crucial reference files from `firebase-integration-rpc` and `frontend-design`. I\'ve also added our project files to the mix. The goal is a comprehensive understanding of the existing structure.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firebase rules & blueprint reference\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Firebase rules reference\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/3_saas_dashboard.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading SaaS dashboard design reference\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read SaaS dashboard reference\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading current Firebase blueprint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading current Firestore security rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read firestore.rules\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":177,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:35:11Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":23695,\"cache_read_tokens\":89067,\"output_tokens\":351,\"thinking\":\"**Integrating Existing Files**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on ensuring a smooth integration for Phase 2. I\'m taking a close look at our core data and UI files to prevent any duplicated patterns or breaking changes. I\'m specifically examining `/src/data/repositories/interfaces.ts` and `/src/data/repositories/firebaseWebAdapter.ts` to identify potential areas of overlap and ensure seamless compatibility.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/repositories/interfaces.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading repository interfaces\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read repository interfaces\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/repositories/firebaseWebAdapter.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firebase web adapter\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Firebase web adapter\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading App root component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read App.tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/AppShell.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading AppShell component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read AppShell.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":182,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:35:24Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":12479,\"cache_read_tokens\":112763,\"output_tokens\":306,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/home/ui/HomeView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading HomeView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read HomeView.tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/core/currency/currency.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading currency utilities\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read currency.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/core/i18n/i18n.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading i18n translations\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read i18n.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/state/useUIStore.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading UI store\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read useUIStore.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/hooks/useLifeOS.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading useLifeOS hooks\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read useLifeOS.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":188,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:35:38Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":130144,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":209,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/core/ai/llmProvider.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading LLM provider interface\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read llmProvider.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firestore.indexes.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firestore indexes\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read firestore.indexes.json\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firestore security rules tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read firestore.rules.test.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":192,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:36:08Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":134823,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":5471,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Phase 2 Debts**\\n\\nI\'m now carefully designing Phase 2, focusing on principal-architect precision. I\'m reviewing the approved architecture and vision documents to pinpoint every required capability, starting with data models and Firestore security rules. My aim is to build a robust and secure foundation for the debts manager.\\n\\n\\n**Addressing Data Schema Gaps**\\n\\nI\'m expanding the data model with `DebtRecord`, `DebtLedger`, and a `DebtPayment` subcollection. The new `DebtRecord` schema will have fiel\\n<truncated 4660 bytes>\\nerparty, direction, progress, and quick actions. The UI will support EN/AR/CKB RTL on both desktop and mobile.\\n\\n\\n**Building Interactive Components**\\n\\nI\'m now building the interactive modal for debt management. I am developing an \\\"Add/Edit Debt\\\" modal, a \\\"Log Payment/Settle\\\" modal, and a \\\"Debt Detail & Payment History\\\" drawer. These modals will include accessible designs and zero-flicker behavior. I am also working on an AI-powered reminder message drafter modal, enabling language and tone customization.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Enrich DebtLedger and DebtRecord schemas and add DebtPayment entity and subcollection path in firebase-blueprint.json for Phase 2 Debts Manager.\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"111\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update DebtLedger and DebtRecord entity definitions and add DebtPayment entity definition.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"DebtLedger\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DebtLedger\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Denormalized per-person multi-currency ledger totals and repayment reliability.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"uid\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"stri\\n<truncated 4137 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"75\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"DebtLedger\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DebtLedger\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Denormalized per-person multi-currency ledger totals.\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"uid\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"minLength\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"\\n<truncated 2075 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Debt schemas in firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update Debt schemas in blueprint\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":194,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:37:26Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":141994,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":75,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Path and Draft**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating the `/users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}/payments/{paymentId}` path into `firebase-blueprint.json` simultaneously drafting an updated `DRAFT_firestore.rules`. The Eight-Pillar workflow guides my actions, ensuring a structured progression: draft, ESLint, finalize `firestore.rules`, and finally, DeployRules. I\'m focusing on efficiency.\\n\\n\\n\"}\n{\"step_index\":195,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:38:11Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":141994,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":7543,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Firestore Paths**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating the `/users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}/payments/{paymentId}` path into `firestore` within `/firebase-blueprint.json`. Simultaneously, I\'m drafting `/DRAFT_firestore.rules` to enforce the Eight-Pillar hardened rules, ensuring they precisely mirror the structure defined in `firebase-blueprint.json`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Register /users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}/payments/{paymentId} subcollection path in firebase-blueprint.json.\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"276\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add DebtPayment subcollection path right after debts path.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"/users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"$ref\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"#/entities/DebtRecord\\\\\\\" },\\\\n      \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User debt items.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"/users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}/payments/{paymentId}\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"$ref\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"#/e\\n<truncated 128 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"266\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    \\\\\\\"/users/{userId}/debts/{debtId}\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"$ref\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"#/entities/DebtRecord\\\\\\\" },\\\\n      \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User debt items.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firebase-blueprint.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding DebtPayment path to blueprint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add DebtPayment path to blueprint\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"rules_version = \'2\';\\\\n\\\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\\\n\\\\n    // 1. Global Default-Deny Safety Net\\\\n    match /{document=**} {\\\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    // 2. Hardened Global Primitives\\\\n    fu\\n<truncated 25401 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Draft hardened Eight-Pillar Firestore Security Rules for Phase 2 Debts Manager including action-split debt updates and immutable payments subcollection.\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/DRAFT_firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Drafting Phase 2 Firestore security rules\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Draft Phase 2 Firestore rules\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":198,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:39:49Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":149987,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":104,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx eslint DRAFT_firestore.rules\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Auditing Draft Firestore rules with ESLint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Audit Draft Firestore rules\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":200,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:40:59Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":150183,\"cache_read_tokens\":15261,\"output_tokens\":8529,\"thinking\":\"**Confirming Security Rules**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report that the Firebase security rules linting check came back clean, no errors or warnings. Before we declare victory, I\'m shifting focus to our Red Team Audit, specifically on `DRAFT_firestore.rules`. My current goal is the Shadow Update Test, verifying that `isValidDebtRecord` correctly enforces the `hasOnly(...)` and `affectedKeys().hasOnly(...)` split.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Debt Immutability**\\n\\nI am now delving into the intricacies of payment immutability and its \\n<truncated 411 bytes>\\ntion and `affectedKeys()`.\\n\\n\\n**Addressing Debt Status Edge Cases**\\n\\nI\'m now wrestling with several edge cases. I\'ve realized that a debt with `remainingMinor == principalMinor` and a past `dueDate` can be \\\"overdue\\\", bypassing the intended `status` check. Also, a full payment scenario where `amountMinor == remainingMinor` can lead to a \\\"settled\\\" status and pass the checks. I am currently examining the undo behavior and how it impacts re-creating a debt after deletion. I am ready to promote and deploy now.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"rules_version = \'2\';\\\\n\\\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\\\n\\\\n    // 1. Global Default-Deny Safety Net\\\\n    match /{document=**} {\\\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    // 2. Hardened Global Primitives\\\\n    fu\\n<truncated 25401 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Finalize Phase 2 Eight-Pillar Firestore Security Rules covering enriched debts and append-only payments subcollection.\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Finalizing firestore.rules for Phase 2\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Finalize firestore.rules\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"delete_file\",\"args\":{\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/DRAFT_firestore.rules\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Removing temporary draft rules file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Remove DRAFT_firestore.rules\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Extend Firestore rules test suite to verify Phase 2 DebtPayment subcollection and debt action-split invariants.\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"45\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Assert payments subcollection immutability and debt remainingMinor/status synchronization invariant.\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  assert.match(rules, /existing\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\.status != \'settled\'/);\\\\n  assert.match(rules, /match \\\\\\\\/payments\\\\\\\\/\\\\\\\\{paymentId\\\\\\\\}[\\\\\\\\s\\\\\\\\S]*allow update: if false;/);\\\\n  assert.match(rules, /isValidDebtPayment/);\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ntest(\'firebase-blueprint.json paths are all\\n<truncated 777 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"22\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  assert.match(rules, /existing\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\.status != \'settled\'/);\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\ntest(\'firebase-blueprint.json paths are all covered in firestore.rules\', () => {\\\\n  const rules = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), \'firestore.rules\'), \'utf8\');\\\\n  const blue\\n<truncated 529 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/firestore.rules.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Firestore rules test assertions\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update firestore.rules.test.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":204,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-23T20:42:40Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":2889,\"cache_read_tokens\":171789,\"output_tokens\":184,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx eslint firestore.rules\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"Wai