  planner_response {
    response: "**Phase 3 \342\200\224 Smart Reminders & Notification Scheduler** is complete and verified.\n\n### What Was Built\n- **RFC-5545 Recurrence Engine (Expo-portable)**: Full RRULE parser, serializer, human-readable formatter, month-end clamping (e.g., Jan 31 \342\206\222 Feb 28/29 \342\206\222 Mar 31), and automatic next-occurrence advancement on completion (supporting `DAILY`, `WEEKLY` with weekdays, `MONTHLY`, `YEARLY`, custom `INTERVAL`, and `COUNT` limits).\n- **Rolling 64-Notification Scheduler & Quiet Hours**:\n  - Enforces the iOS 64-pending-local-notification cap across a rolling 30-day horizon, merging active reminders with open Debt due-date alerts.\n  - Automatically detects overnight and daytime Quiet Hours from user settings, shifting standard alerts to the end of Quiet Hours while allowing opt-out bypass for urgent channels like **Medicine**.\n  - Includes browser `Notification` API permission & test dispatch in the Web/PWA view, with an explicit transparency note that closed-app background alarms require native Expo EAS builds or server push (FCM).\n- **8 Dedicated Notification Channels**: `Routine`, `Medicine`, `Debt`, `Bill`, `Expiry`, `Birthday`, `Task`, and `Custom` \342\200\224 each with channel-specific default priorities, quiet-hour policies, and quick agenda filtering.\n- **7-Day Workload Balance & Agenda Controls**: Deterministic daily overload analysis (flagging days with \342\211\2455 alerts or \342\211\2453 alerts in a single hour), one-tap Complete/Reopen, inline Snooze presets (`+15m`, `+1h`, `Tomorrow 09:00`), optional links to open debts, and Delete with Undo.\n- **Privacy-Gated AI Quick Schedule (`EN \302\267 AR \302\267 CKB`)**: Natural-language schedule parser routed through the server-side Gemini proxy with prompt-injection delimiters, daily quota enforcement, and confirmation-gated editable draft previews.\n- **Hardened Cloud Firestore Rules & Offline Parity**: Updated schema and action-split security rules (separate Create, Complete/Advance, Snooze, and Edit validation plus terminal archive lock) deployed to your Firebase project, alongside seamless offline local persistence and live Home dashboard KPI integration.\n\n### Verification\n- **26 / 26 unit tests passing** across Reminders (RRULE, month-end clamping, quiet hours, 64-slot cap, recurring advancement, 7-day workload), Debts, Currency, Privacy Gate, Entitlements, and Firestore rule invariants.\n- **End-to-end browser verification** passed with 0 console errors and 0 warnings, followed by clean TypeScript type-checking and production build.\n- Please take a moment to review the updated `firestore.rules` in your project to verify the access-control logic matches your expectations.\n\n---\n\n**Ready for Phase 4 (Planner & Rich Markdown Notes)** \342\200\224 fractional-index task ordering, subtasks, unified calendar view, AI goal breakdown, nested Markdown note folders, version history, and opt-in AES-256-GCM locked notes. Reply **\"Proceed to Phase 4\"** whenever you\'re ready."
    thinking: "**Confirming System Integrity**\n\nI\'ve got good news: all 26 unit tests completed without any failures. The tests covered a wide range of critical functionalities, including recurrent rules, month-end adjustments, and system overload management. Also, I have verified our Firestore rules are well-structured and ESLint audited.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "ELEEa5WXLbT7-sAP4tj08Qs"
    modified_response: "**Phase 3 \342\200\224 Smart Reminders & Notification Scheduler** is complete and verified.\n\n### What Was Built\n- **RFC-5545 Recurrence Engine (Expo-portable)**: Full RRULE parser, serializer, human-readable formatter, month-end clamping (e.g., Jan 31 \342\206\222 Feb 28/29 \342\206\222 Mar 31), and automatic next-occurrence advancement on completion (supporting `DAILY`, `WEEKLY` with weekdays, `MONTHLY`, `YEARLY`, custom `INTERVAL`, and `COUNT` limits).\n- **Rolling 64-Notification Scheduler & Quiet Hours**:\n  - Enforces the iOS 64-pending-local-notification cap across a rolling 30-day horizon, merging active reminders with open Debt due-date alerts.\n  - Automatically detects overnight and daytime Quiet Hours from user settings, shifting standard alerts to the end of Quiet Hours while allowing opt-out bypass for urgent channels like **Medicine**.\n  - Includes browser `Notification` API permission & test dispatch in the Web/PWA view, with an explicit transparency note that closed-app background alarms require native Expo EAS builds or server push (FCM).\n- **8 Dedicated Notification Channels**: `Routine`, `Medicine`, `Debt`, `Bill`, `Expiry`, `Birthday`, `Task`, and `Custom` \342\200\224 each with channel-specific default priorities, quiet-hour policies, and quick agenda filtering.\n- **7-Day Workload Balance & Agenda Controls**: Deterministic daily overload analysis (flagging days with \342\211\2455 alerts or \342\211\2453 alerts in a single hour), one-tap Complete/Reopen, inline Snooze presets (`+15m`, `+1h`, `Tomorrow 09:00`), optional links to open debts, and Delete with Undo.\n- **Privacy-Gated AI Quick Schedule (`EN \302\267 AR \302\267 CKB`)**: Natural-language schedule parser routed through the server-side Gemini proxy with prompt-injection delimiters, daily quota enforcement, and confirmation-gated editable draft previews.\n- **Hardened Cloud Firestore Rules & Offline Parity**: Updated schema and action-split security rules (separate Create, Complete/Advance, Snooze, and Edit validation plus terminal archive lock) deployed to your Firebase project, alongside seamless offline local persistence and live Home dashboard KPI integration.\n\n### Verification\n- **26 / 26 unit tests passing** across Reminders (RRULE, month-end clamping, quiet hours, 64-slot cap, recurring advancement, 7-day workload), Debts, Currency, Privacy Gate, Entitlements, and Firestore rule invariants.\n- **End-to-end browser verification** passed with 0 console errors and 0 warnings, followed by clean TypeScript type-checking and production build.\n- Please take a moment to review the updated `firestore.rules` in your project to verify the access-control logic matches your expectations.\n\n---\n\n**Ready for Phase 4 (Planner & Rich Markdown Notes)** \342\200\224 fractional-index task ordering, subtasks, unified calendar view, AI goal breakdown, nested Markdown note folders, version history, and opt-in AES-256-GCM locked notes. Reply **\"Proceed to Phase 4\"** whenever you\'re ready."
