    end_line: 686
    content: "---\nname: \"gemini-api\"\ndescription: >\n  Provides model selection guidance and coding patterns for the @google/genai\n  TypeScript SDK. Use when the application requires AI capabilities (e.g.,\n  text/image/music generation, audio transcription, smart features) or when the\n  task involves implementing an \"AI-powered\" feature. The model should prefer\n  this modern SDK over legacy alternatives. Do NOT use for general discussions\n  about AI without implementation intent. Covers model aliases, streaming, chat,\n  function calling, search and maps grounding, image generation, music\n  generation (Lyria), audio transcription, TTS, Live API, and API key handling.\n---\n\n## @google/genai Models\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> The models listed in this section are the absolute source of truth when\n> selecting a model. Even if a specific use case is not listed in the examples\n> or sections below, you must still choose one of the models defined here,\n> unless the user specifies one.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **NEVER** use the following deprecated models. They are strictly prohibited\n> and unsupported: - `gemini-1.5-flash` - `gemini-1.5-pro` - `gemini-pro` -\n> `gemini-2.0-flash` - `gemini-2.0-pro` - `gemini-2.0-flash-thinking`\n>\n> Always select a valid model from the list below.\n\n-   If the user provides a full model name that includes hyphens, a version, and\n    an optional date (e.g., gemini-2.5-flash-preview-12-2025 or\n    gemini-3.1-pro-preview), use it directly.\n-   If the user provides a common name or alias, use the following full model\n    name.\n    -   gemini flash, gemini 4 flash, gemini hydrogen, or gemini 4 hydrogen:\n        \'gemini-4-hydrogen\'\n    -   gemini lite or flash lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'\n    -   gemini carbon or gemini 4 carbon: \'gemini-4-carbon\'\n    -   gemini pro, gemini 4, gemini neon, or gemini 4 neon: \'gemini-4-neon\'\n    -   gemini argon or gemini 4 argon: \'gemini-4-argon\'\n    -   nano banana, or gemini flash image, or nano banana lite, or nano banana\n        2 lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   nano banana 2.1: \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   nano banana pro, or gemini pro image: \'gemini-3-pro-image\'\n    -   native audio, gemini live, or gemini flash audio: \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   gemini live extended thinking or thinker talker:\n        \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   gemini transcribe or audio transcription: \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   live transcribe or live audio transcription:\n        \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   live translate or live speech translation:\n        \'gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview\'\n    -   gemini tts, gemini text-to-speech, or gemini flash lite tts:\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   gemini flash tts: \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   gemini omni flash, Veo, or Veo lite: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\'\n    -   genie, genie 4, or interactive world model: \'genie-4\'\n    -   Lyria Clip: \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Lyria Pro: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n    -   gemini embedding or gemini embedding 2: \'gemini-embedding-2\'\n    -   gemini decision, gemini decision 1, or decisions api:\n        \'gemini-decision-1\'\n-   If the user does not specify any model, select the following model based on\n    the task type.\n    -   Basic Text Tasks (e.g., summarization, proofreading, and simple Q&A):\n        \'gemini-4-hydrogen\'\n    -   Complex Text Tasks (e.g., advanced reasoning, coding, math, and STEM):\n        \'gemini-4-neon\'\n    -   Deep Reasoning Tasks pushing reasoning depth (e.g., complex root-cause\n        debugging, architectural design, scientific proofs, and security\n        auditing): \'gemini-4-carbon\'\n    -   General Image Generation and Editing Tasks:\n        \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   High-Quality Image Generation and Editing Tasks (supports 1K, 2K, and 4K\n        resolution): \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   Video Generation, Editing, and Extension Tasks: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\'\n    -   Real-time Interactive World Generation & Simulation Tasks (720p @ 24 fps\n        video + 48 kHz stereo audio via Live Interactions API): \'genie-4\'\n    -   Audio Transcription Tasks (pre-recorded or static audio via\n        generateContent): \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   Real-time audio & video conversation tasks (via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   Real-time voice conversation tasks requiring complex reasoning or\n        multi-step tool use (via Live API): \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   Real-time live audio transcription tasks (speech-to-text via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   Real-time speech-to-speech translation tasks (via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview\'\n    -   General Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g., article reading, global\n        dubbing/localization, customer service IVR, accessibility screen\n        readers, and high-throughput voice assistants):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   Voice Design, Screenplay, and Podcasting Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g.,\n        prompting custom voice personas from scratch, dual-speaker screenplay\n        editing, and dialogue apps requiring backchanneling like `|mhm|` or\n        `|yeah|` and vocal bursts like `<laugh>` or `<gasp>`):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   Short music clip generation tasks (30s): \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Full-length music generation tasks: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n    -   Embedding tasks: \'gemini-embedding-2\'\n    -   Calibrated yes/no checks, multi-class routing/classification, policy\n        checks, or rubric scoring tasks (via Decisions API): \'gemini-decision-1\'\n\nThe following models require a paid API key. Prompt the user to select one by\ncalling the `show_aistudio_ui` tool with arguments: `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"`\n*before* using these models.\n\n-   `gemini-4-carbon`\n-   `gemini-4-neon`\n-   `gemini-4-argon`\n-   `gemini-3-pro-image`\n-   `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`\n-   `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`\n-   `gemini-omni-1.2-flash`\n-   `genie-4`\n-   `lyria-3-clip-preview`\n-   `lyria-3-pro-preview`\n\n# Gemini API guidance\n\n## @google/genai Coding Guidelines\n\nUse the `@google/genai` SDK to call Gemini models.\n\n### Calling Gemini API\n\n**Always** call Gemini API from the server-side code of the application (except\nthe `genie-4` ephemeral-token WebRTC browser client in\n`../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md`). **NEVER** call\nGemini API directly from the client/browser code with `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n**NEVER** expose the API key to the browser.\n\nThe server handles all `@google/genai` SDK calls. The client communicates with\nthe server through your application\'s API endpoints (e.g., Next.js API routes,\nExpress routes, or Angular SSR endpoints).\n\nIf a server-side Gemini call fails or errors, propagate the error back to the\nclient (via the HTTP response, SSE stream, or WebSocket) so the frontend can\ndisplay it.\n\n### Migrating Gemini API Calls to Server-Side\n\nWhen the user prompts an update to add or change Gemini capabilities in an\nexisting app that has client-side Gemini API calls, you should migrate the code\nto the server side as part of your response unless the user specifically\nrequested to keep it on the client side.\n\nIf the migration involves models that require a paid API key, refer to the \"Paid\nAPI Key\" section for instructions on how to prompt the user.\n\nWhen migrating client-side Gemini API calls to server-side:\n\n-   You must remove any legacy client-side key selection methods such as\n    `window.aistudio.hasSelectedApiKey()` and `window.aistudio.openSelectKey()`.\n-   You must remove any legacy `define` entries for `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`\n    or `process.env.API_KEY` (and `loadEnv(mode, \'.\', \'\')` if no longer used)\n    from `vite.config.ts`.\n-   Explain the change positively. Frame it as an upgrade or improvement, not a\n    fix.\n-   Do not include security justifications like \"preventing exposure to the\n    browser\" in the response.\n\n**Example response:** \"I\'ve updated your app\'s Gemini API calls to our\nrecommended approach for full-stack apps. You can see your app\'s attached API\nkey in the **Settings > Secrets** panel.\"\n\n**DO say:**\n\n-   \"We\'ve updated your app\'s Gemini API calls\"\n-   \"Your API key can be found in the **Settings > Secrets** panel.\"\n-   \"We\'ve set up your API key automatically\"\n\n**DON\'T say:**\n\n-   \"Your API key was exposed\" / \"insecure\"\n-   \"The old method is deprecated\"\n-   \"You need to migrate\" / \"breaking change\"\n-   \"Your app needs to be fixed\"\n-   \"This prevents the API key from being exposed to the browser\"\n\n**Metadata Update:** You must update the application\'s metadata file to include\nthe major server capability:\n`\"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]`.\n\n### Server-Side Initialization\n\nCreate a shared Gemini client utility on the server. You **must** set the\n`User-Agent` header to `\'aistudio-build\'` in `httpOptions` for telemetry.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\nconst ai = new GoogleGenAI({\n  apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY,\n  httpOptions: {\n    headers: {\n      \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\',\n    }\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Client-Side Usage\n\nThe client never imports `@google/genai` (except the `genie-4` ephemeral-token\nWebRTC client in `../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md`,\nwhich never receives `GEMINI_API_KEY`). Instead, it calls your server\'s API\nroutes, for example:\n\n```ts\nconst response = await fetch(\"/api/gemini/generate\", {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: userInput }),\n});\nconst data = await response.json();\n```\n\n### Incorrect Usages\n\nDo *not* use or import the following types from `@google/genai`; these are\ndeprecated APIs and no longer work.\n\n-   **Incorrect** `GoogleGenerativeAI`\n-   **Incorrect** `google.generativeai`\n-   **Incorrect** `models.create`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models.create`\n-   **Incorrect** `models.getGenerativeModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `genAI.getGenerativeModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models.getModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models[\'model_name\']`\n-   **Incorrect** `generationConfig`\n-   **Incorrect** `GoogleGenAIError`\n-   **Incorrect** `GenerateContentResult`; **Correct**\n    `GenerateContentResponse`.\n-   **Incorrect** `GenerateContentRequest`; **Correct**\n    `GenerateContentParameters`.\n-   **Incorrect** `SchemaType`; **Correct** `Type`.\n\nDo *not* import `@google/genai` or instantiate `GoogleGenAI` in any client-side\n/ browser code unless using the `genie-4` ephemeral-token WebRTC client\n(`../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md`) or when the user\nexplicitly asks for it (in which case highlight the security implications of\nexposing an API key). All Gemini SDK usage must be server-side by default.\n\nWhen using generate content for text answers, do *not* define the model first\nand call generate content later. You must use `ai.models.generateContent` to\nquery GenAI with both the model name and prompt.\n\n### API Key\n\n-   **Server-only:** The API key is accessed via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` on\n    the server. It must **never** be sent to the browser or included in\n    client-side bundles.\n\n-   **Incorrect Initialization:** `const ai = new GoogleGenAI(apiKey);` // Must\n    use a named parameter `{ apiKey: ... }`.\n\n-   **No UI for API Key:** Do **not** generate any UI elements (input fields,\n    forms, prompts, configuration sections) or code snippets for entering or\n    managing the API key. Do **not** request that the user update the API key in\n    the code. The key\'s availability is handled externally and is a hard\n    requirement. The application **must not** ask the user for it under any\n    circumstances.\n\n### Paid API Key\n\nSome models require a paid API key (see the list of paid models at the top of\nthis file). Prompt the user to select one by calling the `show_aistudio_ui` tool\nwith arguments: `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"` *before* using these models.\n\nThe selected API key is available using `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. It is\ninjected automatically, so you do not need to modify the API key code.\n\n### Import\n\n-   **SDK Version:** Ensure `@google/genai` is `>= 2.29.1` in `package.json`\n    (required for `gemini-3.8-*`, `gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-neon`,\n    `gemini-4-carbon`, `gemini-4-argon`, `speechMetadata`,\n    `Behavior.NON_BLOCKING`, and `InteractionStatus`; use `>= 3.3.0` via\n    `npm i @google/genai@latest` for the `ThinkingLevel.XHIGH` enum member; use\n    `>= 3.5.0` with `apiVersion: \"v1beta\"` only when using `genie-4`\n    `ai.interactions.connect` / `ai.interactions.authTokens`). Only run\n    `npm i @google/genai@latest` when the installed version is below the minimum\n    required for the feature in use.\n-   Always use `import {GoogleGenAI} from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `import { GoogleGenerativeAI } from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `import type { GoogleGenAI} from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `declare var GoogleGenAI`.\n-   **Prohibited:** Any `@google/genai` import in client-side code, except the\n    `genie-4` ephemeral-token WebRTC client\n    (`../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md`).\n\n## Specialized Modality & Tool References\n\nCore text and multimodal input generation (`generateContent`,\n`generateContentStream`), system instructions, `thinkingLevel`, structured JSON\n(`responseSchema`), multi-turn `ai.chats`, and error handling are covered\ndirectly below\342\200\224do **not** load reference files when your task only uses these\ncore patterns.\n\nLoad the matching `references/*.md` file in this skill\'s directory (relative to\nthis `SKILL.md` path) using `view_file` **only when** implementing one of these\nspecialized capabilities:\n\n-   **[references/tools_and_grounding.md](references/tools_and_grounding.md)**:\n    Function calling (`FunctionDeclaration`, hybrid built-in + custom tools with\n    `includeServerSideToolInvocations`), Google Search grounding\n    (`googleSearch`), Google Maps grounding (`googleMaps`), URL Context\n    (`urlContext`), and multimodal embeddings (`embedContent`).\n-   **[references/image_video_music.md](references/image_video_music.md)**:\n    Image generation and editing (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`,\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`, `imageConfig`, `imageSearch`), music generation\n    with Lyria (`lyria-3-clip-preview`, `lyria-3-pro-preview`), and video\n    generation/editing routing (`gemini-omni-1.2-flash` via\n    `gemini-interactions-api`).\n-   **[references/speech_and_audio.md](references/speech_and_audio.md)**:\n    Pre-recorded audio transcription (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`) and\n    Text-to-Speech (`gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts` single-speaker and streaming\n    PCM, `gemini-3.8-flash-tts` multi-speaker, Voice Design, backchanneling, and\n    WAV vs. raw PCM output formats).\n-   **[references/live_api.md](references/live_api.md)**: Real-time low-latency\n    voice and video streaming via the Live API (`ai.live.connect`,\n    `gemini-3.8-live`, `gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking`,\n    `gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview` speech translation,\n    `gemini-3.5-transcribe-live` live transcription, WebSocket bridging, and\n    16kHz input / 24kHz output PCM rules).\n-   **[../gemini_interactions_api/references/decisions-api.md](../gemini_interactions_api/references/decisions-api.md)**:\n    **Decisions API (`gemini-decision-1`)** \342\200\224 calibrated yes/no (`noul`),\n    single-select (`choice`), and rubric (`score`) evaluations via\n    `ai.decisions.create` (never `generateContent` or `interactions.create`).\n    You **MUST** read this reference file via `view_file` (resolved relative to\n    this `SKILL.md` path; do **not** inspect `node_modules/@google/genai`),\n    upgrade with `npm i @google/genai@latest` (`>= 3.2.0`), initialize `new\n    GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY, apiVersion: \"v1beta\", ...\n    })`, and pass bare `model: \"gemini-decision-1\"`.\n-   **[../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md](../gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md)**:\n    **Interactive World Generation (`models/genie-4`)** \342\200\224 real-time 720p @ 24\n    fps video + 48 kHz stereo audio over the **Live Interactions API**\n    (`v1beta`, `@google/genai >= 3.5.0` via `npm i @google/genai@latest`). You\n    **MUST** read this reference file via `view_file` before implementing Genie\n    4: mint the interaction (`models/genie-4`) and ephemeral auth token\n    (`interactions.authTokens.create`) server-side, connect from the browser via\n    WebRTC `interactions.connect` using only that ephemeral token (never\n    `GEMINI_API_KEY`), send `world_setup`, and always call `session.complete()`\n    on teardown.\n\n## Server-Side API Examples\n\nAll examples below show the server-side `@google/genai` SDK usage. Expose these\nas API endpoints in your framework of choice (Next.js API routes, Express\nroutes, etc.).\n\n### Generate Content\n\nGenerate a response from the model.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: \"why is the sky blue?\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\nGenerate content with multiple parts, for example, by sending an image and a\ntext prompt to the model.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, GenerateContentResponse } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst imagePart = {\n  inlineData: {\n    // Could be any other IANA standard MIME type for the source data.\n    mimeType: \"image/png\",\n    data: base64EncodeString,\n  },\n};\nconst textPart = {\n  text: promptString, // text prompt\n};\nconst response: GenerateContentResponse = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: { parts: [imagePart, textPart] },\n});\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\n### Extracting Text Output from `GenerateContentResponse`\n\nWhen you use `ai.models.generateContent`, it returns a `GenerateContentResponse`\nobject. The simplest and most direct way to get the generated text content is by\naccessing the `.text` property on this object.\n\n#### Correct Method\n\nThe `GenerateContentResponse` object features a `text` property (not a method,\nso do not call `text()`) that directly returns the string output.\n\nProperty definition:\n\n```ts\nexport class GenerateContentResponse {\n ......\n\n get text(): string | undefined {\n // Returns the extracted string output.\n }\n}\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\nimport { Chat, GoogleGenAI, GenerateContentResponse } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response: GenerateContentResponse = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: \"why is the sky blue?\",\n});\nconst text = response.text; // Do not use response.text()\nconsole.log(text);\n\nconst chat: Chat = ai.chats.create({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n});\nlet streamResponse = await chat.sendMessageStream({\n  message: \"Tell me a story in 100 words.\",\n});\nfor await (const chunk of streamResponse) {\n  const c = chunk as GenerateContentResponse;\n  console.log(c.text); // Do not use c.text()\n}\n```\n\n### Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n-   **Incorrect:** `const text = response.text();`\n-   **Incorrect:** `const text = response?.response?.text?;`\n-   **Incorrect:** `const text = response?.response?.text();`\n-   **Incorrect:** `const text = response?.response?.text?.()?.trim();`\n-   **Incorrect:**\n    `const json = response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.json;`\n\n### System Instruction and Other Model Configs\n\nGenerate a response with a system instruction and other model configs.\n\nNote: The `maxOutputTokens` parameter includes both response tokens and thinking\n(reasoning) tokens. It is recommended to specify the desired response size\nwithin the `systemInstruction` rather than using `maxOutputTokens`. Do not pass\ndeprecated sampling parameters (`temperature`, `topP`, `topK`) or\n`candidateCount` to `gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-neon`, `gemini-4-argon`, or\n`gemini-4-carbon`.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: \"Tell me a story.\",\n  config: {\n    systemInstruction: \"You are a storyteller for kids under 5 years old.\",\n    responseMimeType: \"application/json\",\n    seed: 42,\n  },\n});\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\n### Thinking Level\n\n-   The `thinkingLevel` parameter controls the model\'s reasoning behavior. It is\n    only available for Gemini 3 and Gemini 4 series models. Do not use it with\n    other models. Pass uppercase `ThinkingLevel` enum members (do **not** pass\n    raw lowercase strings like `\"xhigh\"` to `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel` in\n    TypeScript):\n    -   `ThinkingLevel.XHIGH`: Maximum reasoning depth on `\'gemini-4-neon\'` and\n        `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'` for complex, multi-step agentic workflows,\n        open-ended research, and multi-document synthesis. **Only** supported on\n        `\'gemini-4-neon\'` and `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'` \342\200\224 **not** supported on\n        `\'gemini-4-argon\'`, `\'gemini-4-carbon\'`, or Gemini 3 models (returns a\n        400 error). Requires `@google/genai >= 3.3.0`\n        (`npm i @google/genai@latest`; if an older `2.29.1`\342\200\223`3.2.0` package is\n        installed, upgrade or use `\'XHIGH\' as ThinkingLevel`).\n    -   `ThinkingLevel.HIGH` (Default for `\'gemini-4-neon\'` and\n        `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'`): Balanced intelligence and speed on\n        `\'gemini-4-neon\'` and `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'`, and maximum reasoning depth\n        on `\'gemini-4-argon\'`, `\'gemini-4-carbon\'`, and Gemini 3 models.\n    -   `ThinkingLevel.MEDIUM` (Default for `\'gemini-4-argon\'` and\n        `\'gemini-4-carbon\'`): Balances reasoning depth with latency and cost\n        (faster responses and lower token use than the default `\'HIGH\'` on\n        `\'gemini-4-neon\'` and `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'`).\n    -   `ThinkingLevel.LOW`: Minimizes latency and cost.\n    -   `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`: Equivalent to no thinking. Default for\n        `\'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'`. **Not** supported on `\'gemini-4-neon\'`,\n        `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'`, `\'gemini-4-argon\'`, or `\'gemini-4-carbon\'`\n        (returns a 400 error).\n-   **Do NOT** set `thinkingBudget` for `\'gemini-4-neon\'`,\n    `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'`, `\'gemini-4-argon\'`, or `\'gemini-4-carbon\'`. It is not\n    supported and the request fails with a 400 error. Use `thinkingLevel`\n    instead.\n-   By default, you do not need to set `thinkingLevel`, as the model\n    automatically decides the amount of reasoning based on the complexity of the\n    requests.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, ThinkingLevel } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: \"Provide a list of 3 famous physicists and their key contributions\",\n  // Use ThinkingLevel.LOW for lowest latency, or ThinkingLevel.XHIGH for max reasoning on gemini-4-neon / gemini-4-hydrogen\n  config: { thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW } }\n});\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\n### JSON Response\n\nAsk the model to return a response in JSON format.\n\nThe recommended way is to configure a `responseSchema` for the expected output.\n\nSee the following available types that can be used in the `responseSchema`.\n\n```ts\nexport enum Type {\n  TYPE_UNSPECIFIED = \"TYPE_UNSPECIFIED\",\n  STRING = \"STRING\",\n  NUMBER = \"NUMBER\",\n  INTEGER = \"INTEGER\",\n  BOOLEAN = \"BOOLEAN\",\n  ARRAY = \"ARRAY\",\n  OBJECT = \"OBJECT\",\n  NULL = \"NULL\",\n}\n```\n\n-   Type.OBJECT cannot be empty; it must contain other properties.\n-   Do not use `SchemaType`, it is not available from `@google/genai`\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents:\n    \"List a few popular cookie recipes, and include the amounts of\" +\n      \" ingredients.\",\n  config: {\n    responseMimeType: \"application/json\",\n    responseSchema: {\n      type: Type.ARRAY,\n      items: {\n        type: Type.OBJECT,\n        properties: {\n          recipeName: {\n            type: Type.STRING,\n            description: \"The name of the recipe.\",\n          },\n          ingredients: {\n            type: Type.ARRAY,\n            items: {\n              type: Type.STRING,\n            },\n            description: \"The ingredients for the recipe.\",\n          },\n        },\n        // propertyOrdering is optional\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nconst jsonStr = (response.text ?? \"[]\").trim();\n// Parse jsonStr to get the object\n```\n\n### Generate Content (Streaming)\n\nGenerate a response from the model in streaming mode. Stream the chunks back to\nthe client using Server-Sent Events (SSE) or your framework\'s streaming\nmechanism.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  contents: \"Tell me a story in 300 words.\",\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of response) {\n  console.log(chunk.text);\n  // Write each chunk to your response stream (SSE, WebSocket, etc.)\n}\n```\n\n### Chat\n\nStarts a chat and sends a message to the model.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, GenerateContentResponse } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst chat = ai.chats.create({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  config: {\n    systemInstruction: \"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n  },\n});\n\nlet response: GenerateContentResponse = await chat.sendMessage({\n  message: \"Hello\",\n});\nconsole.log(response.text);\n\nresponse = await chat.sendMessage({ message: \"How are you?\" });\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\n-   `chat.sendMessage` only accepts the `message` parameter, do not use\n    `contents`.\n\n### Chat (Streaming)\n\n```ts\nimport { GenerateContentResponse } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization (using `chat` created via `ai.chats.create(...)`) ...\n\nlet response = await chat.sendMessageStream({\n  message: \"Tell me a long story.\",\n});\nfor await (const chunk of response) {\n  const c = chunk as GenerateContentResponse;\n  console.log(c.text); // Do not use c.text()\n}\n```\n\n-   `chat.sendMessageStream` only accepts the `message` parameter, do not use\n    `contents`.\n\n### API Error Handling\n\n-   Implement robust handling for API errors (e.g., network issues, 4xx/5xx\n    responses).\n-   Use graceful retry logic (like exponential backoff) to avoid overwhelming\n    the backend and improve reliability.\n-   Return meaningful error responses from API endpoints so the client can\n    display appropriate messages. Never silently mask missing-key or upstream\n    API errors with simulated, heuristic, or hardcoded model outputs.\n-   If you receive a `PERMISSION_DENIED` (403) or `API_KEY_INVALID` (400) error\n    from the Gemini API, or if the user reports this error in their application,\n    ask the user to check the API key (or select one if not set) in the\n    **Settings > Secrets** panel.\n-   If you receive a `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (429) error while using a free tier\n    api key, it might be because you are accessing a paid-only model. Advise the\n    user that upgrading to a paid tier increases their quota, and that they can\n    use the **Settings > Secrets** panel to select a billing enabled API key.\n-   If you encounter a `NOT_FOUND` (404) error when calling the Gemini API, or\n    if the user reports a 404 error, it typically indicates that the requested\n    model is invalid or unsupported. You **MUST** verify and update the model\n    name to one of the active models defined in the **## @google/genai Models**\n    section.\n"
