  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Phase 4 Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into Phase 4: Planner and Rich Markdown Notes. I\'m focusing on the data model and hardening Firestore security rules, building a solid foundation for tasks, unified calendars, and note-taking functionality. I am mapping out the architecture in detail before any coding starts.\n\n\n**Enumerating Phase 4 Entities**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the `TaskItem` entity for Phase 4. I\'ve fleshed out its fields, including `uid`, `listId`, `title`, `notes`, `priority`, `sortKey` (using lexicographic fractional indexing for efficient reordering), `status`, `dueDate`, and a placeholder for subtasks pending Pillar 5. I\'m ensuring data integrity with validation rules, paying close attention to data types and constraints.\n\n\n**Refining Task Updates**\n\nI\'ve specified action-based updates for tasks. Reordering will exclusively modify `sortKey`, `listId`, `version`, and `updatedAt`. Status/Subtasks progress will only touch `status`, `subtasks`, `completedAtIso`, `version`, and `updatedAt`. Edit Metadata affects  `listId`, `title`, `notes`, `priority`, `dueDate`, `subtasks`, and `tags`. This ensures controlled data modification. I\'ve also added strict validation to the array of subtasks, tags, ensuring that the number is bounded (subtasks <= 20, tags <= 10).\n\n\n**Defining Note Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now detailing `NoteFolder` and `NoteItem` entities.  For `NoteFolder`, I\'m working out nested folder structures with `parentId` and validation rules. `NoteItem` is next, and the focus is encryption strategy for sensitive content with AES-256-GCM, along with plain Markdown handling for `content` when `isEncrypted` is false. I\'m also ensuring robust validation rules.\n\n\n**Specifying Note Actions**\n\nI\'m currently formalizing update actions for notes. I have defined an array of fields that can be updated for Pin/Move operations. Lock/Unlock operations require content and encryption flags. Editing note content and metadata will update all related fields. Data validation for all of these actions is paramount.\n\n\n**Formalizing Note History**\n\nI\'m now detailing note versioning. Each immutable snapshot includes `uid`, `noteId`, `title`, `content`, `isEncrypted`, `versionNumber`, and `createdAt`. This append-only system allows users to view and revert to past versions. I am focusing on the Master Gate checks, validating parent note existence, ensuring a robust and secure history.\n\n**Defining Indexing Logic**\n\nI have finalized the core engine for fractional indexing for the planner. The engine will use a pure base-62 lexicographic midpoint generator to facilitate the sorting of items in a list. This allows efficient inserting between items. I have handles for edge cases such as empty lists or prepending items.\n\n\n**Implementing SortKey Generation**\n\nI\'ve been working on a base-62 lexicographic midpoint generator, refining edge case handling where a new `sortKey` needs to be inserted between `prev` and `next`, and also implementing a comparator to sort the items. I am now focused on handling cases where `next` and `prev` are immediately adjacent by extending precision. My primary goal is to maintain the sort order across Javascript and Firestore.\n\n\n**Developing Note Functionality**\n\nI\'ve been working on Zod schemas for `NoteFolder`, `NoteItem`, and `NoteVersion`, along with inputs for creating notes and folders. I have a `countMarkdownWords(text)` helper and a nested hierarchy resolver with cycle protection for folder structures. I\'ve also implemented a safe Markdown parser. It produces AST tokens for different Markdown elements and renders them as native React elements, ensuring zero XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n\n**Testing AI Interactions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on testing the newly implemented AI endpoints. I\'m verifying the functionality of the `breakdown` endpoint, ensuring it correctly processes user goals, passes through the Privacy Gate, and returns a Zod-validated preview of task details. Additionally, I\'m confirming that the `assist` endpoint accurately handles note summarization, action item generation, and content polishing, while strictly enforcing the blocking of locked or encrypted notes. I am checking the round-trip through the privacy gate.\n\n\n**Defining Data Layers**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining data access layers, hooks, and UI components for Planner and Notes. I\'m working on `plannerRepository.ts` and `notesRepository.ts`, which are the entry points for the Firebase and Local offline data sources. I have implemented a memory-only unlocked AES `CryptoKey` map that auto-clears when locking notes or the app for `useNotes.ts` which has built in protection against storing encryption keys to local storage. I\'m also planning the UI components, including the KPIs in a 4-col layout.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the UI components for Phase 4: Planner and Notes. I\'m focusing on features such as a segmented tab for the task board and the unified calendar. I\'m building out a list filter for various list categories (Inbox, Personal, etc.), and adding HTML5 drag-and-drop combined with keyboard accessibility for item reordering, and also an AI Goal Breakdown modal. I\'m working on the Notes components with a nested folder tree and filter, a notes list, and the note editor.\n\n\n**Updating Firestore Rules**\n\nI am now focusing on the infrastructure setup for Phase 4. I am updating `firebase-blueprint.json` and creating `DRAFT_firestore.rules`. I\'m also planning to use ESLint, and a test script for the security rules. I\'ll deploy the rules using rpc_action. My goal is to streamline the deployment process.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "07EEa5eJNdeYkdUP-rCw2Q0"
