  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Firestore Rules**\n\nI successfully ran `npx eslint` on `DRAFT_firestore.rules`, and thankfully, it reported no errors or warnings. Now, I\'m mentally auditing the rules, focusing on a \"Red Team\" approach. I\'m checking for weaknesses, specifically examining the use of `hasAll` and `hasOnly` in `create` operations and `affectedKeys().hasOnly` in `update` operations to ensure data integrity and prevent unauthorized access.\n\n\n**Refining Rule Validation**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the validation logic. I\'ve implemented array guarding to enforce size limits and data type validation for subtasks and tags. I\'ve also added checks for self-parent cycles in note folders and an encrypted/locked invariant for notes, ensuring ciphertext isn\'t stored unlocked. I\'ve also set immutable revision logs. Finally, I\'ve confirmed all prior collections from Phases 1-4 are preserved. My next steps involve incorporating these invariants into the test suite and promoting the draft rules.\n\n\n"
