    thinking: "**Designing the next Phase**\n\nI am now focusing on Phase 6\'s core design. I\'m aiming for clean, Expo-portable engines. My current focus is hardening Firestore rules and implementing `@google/genai` Function Calling for a real server-side experience with `FunctionDeclaration`.\n\n\n**Mapping the Architecture**\n\nMy current emphasis is on mapping the clean architecture for Phase 6, before any coding begins. I am updating my data model and security rules with new fields and collections. I\'m upgrading `HabitItem`, and adding `HabitLogMonth`, `TransactionItem`, `FinanceBudget`, and `SubscriptionItem`. The specification of each are now in-progress.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining data structures. I\'ve specified `HabitLogMonth` with a composite key, storing monthly habit buckets. Key fields include `uid`, `habitId`, `monthKey`, and a `completedDays` array with validation constraints. I am also working on `TransactionItem` specifying fields such as `uid`, `type`, `amountMinor`, and `currency` with field constraints.\n\n\n**Specifying New Data Models**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the new data models. I\'ve defined the properties for `/users/{userId}/transactions/{transactionId}`:  `dateYmd`, `paymentMethod`, `note`, `subscriptionId`, and others. For `/users/{userId}/budgets/{budgetId}`, I\'ve specified `limitMinor`, `currency`, and `monthKey`. Lastly, I\'ve specified the required parameters for `/users/{userId}/subscriptions/{subId}`, including `cadence`, `nextBillingYmd`, and `active`. I\'m starting work on the corresponding Zod schemas for the core engines.\n\n\n**Developing Core Engines**\n\nI\'ve been working on core engine implementations. I have a pure, deterministic streak calculator now supporting both daily and weekly streaks, along with an 84-day heatmap generator. I am implementing a break-pattern analyzer for the system, and will be developing a summary aggregator. I have written unit tests for the habit engine, focusing on streak calculations, monthly bucket toggles, heatmap generation, and break-pattern detection. Finally, I\'ve developed Zod schemas for the finance core.\n\n\n**Implementing Finance Engine**\n\nI\'m now implementing the finance engine and I\'m very focused on currency conversions, ensuring there\'s zero float drift using explicit FX rates. I\'m working on category breakdown and budget progress evaluators to flag budgets as OK, warning, or exceeded, and a subscription burn calculator. I\'m also building a deterministic spending anomaly detector. Finally, I\'m working on safe CSV export and a forgiving CSV import parser. I\'m creating tests for multi-currency cash flow, budget thresholds, CSV import/export, and anomaly detection.\n\n**Global Search & Tool-Calling**\n\nI\'m building out a global search and AI tool calling core. I\'m working on a pure deterministic local cross-module search index to allow global searching across my modules. This will allow for easy retrieval of data from multiple sources.\n\n\n**Integrating AI Tool Calls**\n\nI am now integrating AI tool calls. I\'ve designed a structured executor, `executeLifeOSToolCall`, that maps Gemini FunctionCall invocations to local client workspace snapshots, ensuring end-to-end privacy. I\'m developing a global search engine that redacts E2E-locked content and vault binaries, which are handled by the tool call integration. I\'ve written unit tests to ensure privacy redaction, search ranking, and tool-call execution. I\'m focusing on the server endpoint that will use Function Calling for a two-step tool-calling loop.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Call Logic**\n\nI am now focused on refining the tool call logic for the AI integration. I\'ve designed a two-turn system: The first turn takes user queries and returns `FunctionDeclaration` choices from Gemini, with tools like search, financial summaries, and habit streaks. The second turn synthesizes a grounded answer using results from the executed tools. I\'m also adding endpoints for natural language processing of finance transactions and habit coaching.\n\n\n\n**Adding New Repositories**\n\nI\'m now adding `HabitsRepository` and `FinanceRepository` interfaces, along with their Firebase and local implementations. This includes creating web and offline repositories, which will use local storage for offline data handling. I\'m focusing on strictly aggregated deterministic metrics for habit coaching nudges. I am also implementing a security checklist to maintain robust and secure user data.\n\n\n\n**Designing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating new UI enhancements. I\'m focused on developing real-time UI components like `useHabits` and `useFinance` hooks, and designing tactile check-in buttons with haptic feedback. I\'m adding undo features for both habit and finance operations. I\'m also planning the new 4-column KPI strip for the HabitView.\n\n\n**Designing New Ledger UI**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the Ledger UI design. I\'m focusing on a flat KPI strip for monthly financial figures with dual-currency breakdowns. I\'m creating segmented tabs for Ledger, Budgets, and Subscriptions. I am upgrading the AI Command Palette to include instant local cross-module search and Gemini tool-calling assistance with a visible tool execution display.\n\n\n"
