  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Phase 6 Design**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on designing Phase 6: the habits tracker, personal finance ledger, and global AI tool-calling search. Security is paramount, and I\'m meticulously considering an internal threat model and an architectural plan to ensure robust protection throughout this crucial development.\n\n\n**Refining Firestore Schema**\n\nI\'m currently refining the Firestore schema. I\'m expanding `HabitItem` with various fields for categorization, tracking streaks, and visual customization. Also, I\'m introducing `HabitMonthLog` for monthly bucketed logs. Security is a priority, and I\'m crafting smart Firestore Security Rules to optimize reads and manage data access within the `HabitMonthLog` structure. The aim is to handle complex data with ease.\n\n\n**Analyzing Firestore Transactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the structure of `TransactionItem`. I\'ve added several fields: `type`, `amountMinor`, `currency`, `category`, `merchant`, `dateYmd`, `paymentMethod`, `isRecurring`, `recurrenceCadence`, `note`, `version`, and `createdAt`. This is all designed for the personal finance ledger. The goal is to provide a comprehensive and flexible structure to manage different financial transactions.\n\n\n**Implementing Budget Tracking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `BudgetItem` structure, which includes fields for `uid`, `monthKey`, `category`, and financial details. I\'m following my established eight-pillar rules workflow, starting with `firebase-blueprint.json` and drafting Firestore security rules. My focus is on validation and secure updates.\n\n\n**Developing Habit Analysis Functions**\n\nI\'m now writing core functions to improve habit tracking. I\'m excited about the deterministic `computeHabitStreaks`, which will calculate streaks. I\'m also working on `buildHeatmapGrid`, providing a detailed 84-day view, as well as `analyzeBreakPatterns`, which will look for patterns in the data, and `computeHabitsSummary` which will generate key KPIs for the user. I\'m writing unit tests for all of these functions.\n\n\n**Constructing Finance Schemas**\n\nI\'m currently creating Zod schemas in `financeSchemas.ts` for transactions and budgets, defining categories, and specifying payment methods. I\'m focusing on strict integer calculations within `financeEngine.ts` using `convertMinorUnits` and `formatMoney`. I\'m now crafting `computeMonthlyFinanceSummary` to give a detailed monthly picture. I\'m also preparing `exportTransactionsToCsv` with CSV formula injection protection, as well as CSV parsing.\n\n\n**Designing Search Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `globalSearchEngine.ts`, specifically designing a pure offline search that spans all seven LifeOS modules, prioritizing strict privacy. My design ensures no indexing or returning of decrypted content for locked items, and completely excludes sensitive data before any AI calls, ensuring privacy. I\'m building `buildSafeToolContext` to create a sanitized summary snapshot without sensitive content.\n\n\n**Implementing Gemini Tool Calls**\n\nI\'m now implementing Gemini tool calls on the server. I\'ve built unit tests in `globalSearchEngine.test.ts` to verify cross-module ranking, strict exclusion of sensitive content, and proper tool-call execution. Also, I\'ve integrated Gemini\'s `FunctionDeclaration` pattern using `@google/genai` to call `ai.models.generateContent` with fallback to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`. I\'ve added `/api/ai/tool-search` and used Zod validation with rate limiting. I\'m focusing on ensuring data privacy.\n\n\n**Defining AI Action Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/ai/tool-calls` endpoint. I\'ve designed several AI actions that require confirmation. Specifically, I\'m proposing logging transactions and creating daily habits. These actions return a Zod-validated response, including tool calls and suggested actions, with server-side enforcement of `requiresConfirmation: true` for every mutating action. I\'m also adding