    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":536,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:44:58Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":23759,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":368,\"thinking\":\"**Resuming Phase Verification**\\n\\nI\'m now fully immersed in Phase 5 verification. My primary focus is the Vault UI, meticulously examining the layout, visual elements, and ensuring adherence to zero-pill discipline and clean typography. My goal is to affirm its complete adherence to frontend-design specifications, as established in prior analyses.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx tsx --test src/core/vault/vaultEngine.test.ts src/core/planner/plannerEngine.test.ts src/core/notes/notesEngine.test.ts src/core/reminders/reminderEngine.test.ts src/core/debts/debtEngine.test.ts firestore.rules.test.ts src/core/currency/currency.test\\n<truncated 79 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running unit tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run Phase 5 unit tests\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":540,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:47:51Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":26832,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":278,\"thinking\":\"**Discovering Type Mismatches**\\n\\nI\'ve just found a TypeScipt mismatch using `lint_applet`! It flagged a property name conflict: `containsImageOrFile` versus what\'s used within `PrivacyGateInput` in `src/core/ai/privacyGate.ts`. I\'m now going to dig into the details by inspecting `src/core/ai/privacyGate.ts`, `src/core/vault/vaultEngine.test.ts`, and associated lines in `src/features`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/core/ai/privacyGate.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Privacy Gate types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View privacyGate.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/core/vault/vaultEngine.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing vaultEngine.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View vaultEngine.test.ts\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/VaultView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"345\",\"StartLine\":\"295\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing VaultView Privacy Gate call\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View VaultView.tsx lines 295-345\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":544,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:48:49Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":32939,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":633,\"thinking\":\"**Addressing PrivacyGateInput**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `PrivacyGateInput` component. I\'ve noted the specific checks used: `hasAttachmentImage` and `containsVaultSensitiveDoc`, which aren\'t quite the same as a broader check like `containsImageOrFile`. The plan is to simultaneously address this in both `vaultEngine.test.ts` and `VaultView.tsx`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Use hasAttachmentImage and containsVaultSensitiveDoc in vaultEngine.test.ts PrivacyGateInput call\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"117\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Replace containsImageOrFile with hasAttachmentImage and containsVaultSensitiveDoc\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  const gate = evaluatePrivacyGate({\\\\n    freeTier: true,\\\\n    module: \'vault\',\\\\n    text: \'Extract expiry date from Iraqi passport\',\\\\n    hasAttachmentImage: true,\\\\n    containsVaultSensitiveDoc: true,\\\\n  });\\\\n  assert.equal(gate.allowed, false);\\\\n  asse\\n<truncated 54 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"110\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  const gate = evaluatePrivacyGate({\\\\n    freeTier: true,\\\\n    module: \'vault\',\\\\n    text: \'Extract expiry date from Iraqi passport\',\\\\n    containsImageOrFile: true,\\\\n  });\\\\n  assert.equal(gate.allowed, false);\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/core/vault/vaultEngine.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Fixing PrivacyGateInput property in test\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Fix vaultEngine.test.ts PrivacyGateInput\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Use hasAttachmentImage and containsVaultSensitiveDoc in VaultView.tsx PrivacyGateInput call\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"320\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Replace containsImageOrFile with hasAttachmentImage and containsVaultSensitiveDoc\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    const verdict = evaluatePrivacyGate({\\\\n      freeTier: true,\\\\n      module: \'vault\',\\\\n      text: `${doc.title} ${doc.docType} ${doc.ocrText ?? \'\'}`,\\\\n      hasAttachmentImage: true,\\\\n      containsVaultSensitiveDoc: true,\\\\n      containsLockedOrE2E: \\n<truncated 26 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"311\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    const verdict = evaluatePrivacyGate({\\\\n      freeTier: true,\\\\n      module: \'vault\',\\\\n      text: `${doc.title} ${doc.docType} ${doc.ocrText ?? \'\'}`,\\\\n      containsImageOrFile: true,\\\\n      containsLockedOrE2E: doc.isEncrypted,\\\\n    });\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/VaultView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Fixing PrivacyGateInput property in VaultView\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Fix VaultView.tsx PrivacyGateInput\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":547,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:49:12Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":34202,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":265,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx tsx --test src/core/vault/vaultEngine.test.ts src/core/planner/plannerEngine.test.ts src/core/notes/notesEngine.test.ts src/core/reminders/reminderEngine.test.ts src/core/debts/debtEngine.test.ts firestore.rules.test.ts src/core/currency/currency.test\\n<truncated 79 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running all 36 unit tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run full unit test suite\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":551,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:49:35Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":31682,\"cache_read_tokens\":5371,\"output_tokens\":383,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Build Success**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report that all 36 unit tests have passed, and both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` executed without errors. I\'m now proceeding to verify the live application at `http://localhost:3000` using the Playwright CLI, with the initial step being a check to ensure the dev server is running and `playwright-cli` is accessible, or restarting the dev server if needed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/DocumentScannerModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"260\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DocumentScannerModal selectors\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DocumentScannerModal.tsx\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/DocumentScannerModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"600\",\"StartLine\":\"261\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DocumentScannerModal form fields\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DocumentScannerModal.tsx part 2\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/VaultView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"700\",\"StartLine\":\"346\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing VaultView controls\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View VaultView.tsx lines 346-700\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":555,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:50:40Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":52629,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":116,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/DocumentScannerModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"785\",\"StartLine\":\"601\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DocumentScannerModal metadata form\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DocumentScannerModal.tsx lines 601-785\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":557,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:51:32Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":56045,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1846,\"thinking\":\"**Initiating Testing Strategy**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on streamlining our E2E testing with Playwright. My initial approach involves utilizing `playwright-cli` for a cleaner script. I\'m checking for its readiness, and verifying the dev server is correctly serving our application at `http://localhost:3000`. This will be an iterative process.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"mkdir -p .playwright-cli && node -e \'\\\\nconst fs = require(\\\\\\\"fs\\\\\\\");\\\\n// Create a tiny valid 4x4 PNG for scan upload testing\\\\nconst pngBase64 = \\\\\\\"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAQAAAAECAIAAAAmkwkpAAAADklEQVR42mP8z8DwHwAFBQIAX8jx0gAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\\\\\\\";\\\\nfs.writeFi\\n<truncated 5520 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running Playwright Phase 5 E2E verification\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run Playwright Phase 5 E2E & capture screenshots\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":559,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:54:10Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":60806,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":147,\"thinking\":\"**Discovering a Caching Issue**\\n\\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I identified the root cause: the dev server was serving a cached Vite build, displaying outdated information. Also, `networkidle` timed out due to Vite/HMR or persistent connections. The next action is to restart the dev server to clear the cache.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server for Phase 5 build\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":561,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:55:24Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":61039,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1756,\"thinking\":\"**Executing E2E Tests**\\n\\nI\'ve initiated the Playwright end-to-end flow, utilizing `waitUntil: \\\"domcontentloaded\\\"`. My focus is currently on rigorously testing all Phase 5 Vault features, ensuring comprehensive coverage. I\'m actively capturing three crucial screenshots: `p5_vault_inspector.png`, `p5_vault_locked.png`, and `p5_home_active.png`. I will then clean up localStorage and IndexedDB. Afterwards, I\'ll review the `playwright-cli console` output before a clean browser close.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"playwright-cli run-code \'async (page) => {\\\\n  await page.goto(\\\\\\\"http://localhost:3000\\\\\\\", { waitUntil: \\\\\\\"domcontentloaded\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  await page.evaluate(async () => {\\\\n    localStorage.removeItem(\\\\\\\"lifeos_local_vault_folders_v1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    localStorage.removeIt\\n<truncated 5237 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running Playwright Phase 5 E2E tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run Playwright Phase 5 E2E suite\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":563,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:56:46Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":63125,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1734,\"thinking\":\"**Refining UI Interaction**\\n\\nI\'ve zeroed in on the \\\"Scan / Upload Document\\\" button, noticing its consistent appearance in both the header and empty state. My plan is to use `.first()` on the `getByRole` query to target this button, followed by selecting the \\\"\342\200\224 Passports\\\" folder within the modal. I\'m ready to execute this next.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"playwright-cli run-code \'async (page) => {\\\\n  await page.goto(\\\\\\\"http://localhost:3000\\\\\\\", { waitUntil: \\\\\\\"domcontentloaded\\\\\\\" });\\\\n  await page.evaluate(async () => {\\\\n    localStorage.removeItem(\\\\\\\"lifeos_local_vault_folders_v1\\\\\\\");\\\\n    localStorage.removeIt\\n<truncated 5245 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running Playwright Phase 5 E2E verification\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run Playwright Phase 5 E2E verification\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":565,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:58:13Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":64994,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":202,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Recent Progress**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report complete success with every step leading up to the `p5_vault_inspector.png` stage. I successfully created nested folders, uploaded a sample PNG, rotated it 90 degrees, applied the Doc B&W filter, saved a multi-page PDF to the Vault, scheduled a 30-day expiry reminder, and verified the Privacy Gate\'s `BLOCKED_FREE_TIER_VAULT_IMAGE` status. This is all very encouraging!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/features/vault/ui/VaultView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"860\",\"StartLine\":\"701\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing VaultView inspector action buttons\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View VaultView.tsx lines 701-860\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":567,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:58:28Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":3232,\"cache_read_tokens\":64995,\"output_tokens\":771,\"thinking\":\"**Discovering the Override**\\n\\nI\'ve just found something interesting. It appears that the `aria-label` attribute on line 745, which reads \\\"Encrypt document,\\\" is overriding the accessible name \\\"Lock E2E\\\" for the button with `getByRole`. Because of this I can now use `getByRole(\\\"button\\\", { name: \\\"Encrypt document\\\" })` to locate that button. My next step will be to complete the E2E script.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"playwright-cli run-code \'async (page) => {\\\\n  // Click Encrypt document (Lock E2E)\\\\n  await page.getByRole(\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\", { name: \\\\\\\"Encrypt document\\\\\\\" }).click();\\\\n  await page.waitForSelector(\\\\\\\"text=Enable AES-256-GCM\\\\\\\");\\\\n  const pwInputs = page.locator(\\\\\\\"\\n<truncated 1702 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Completing E2E E2E-lock & Home verification\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Complete Playwright E2E lock, Home & cleanup\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":569,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:58:53Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":72548,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":149,\"thinking\":\"**Inspecting Visual Data**\\n\\nI\'m now deeply immersed in analyzing those screenshots: `p5_vault_locked.png`, `p5_home_active.png`, and `p5_vault_inspector.png`. I\'m using `view_file` to thoroughly audit the visual data. My focus is on zeroing in on any critical features and details I\'ve initially spotted.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.playwright-cli/p5_vault_inspector.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting Vault Inspector screenshot\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect p5_vault_inspector.png\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":571,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:59:02Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":3378,\"cache_read_tokens\":70499,\"output_tokens\":759,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Visual Details**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on the visual design language. The screenshots are remarkably clean and editorial. I\'m noting the 3-pane studio layout, hairline dividers, and the use of a crisp emerald accent. The nested folders, like \\\"Identity\\\" and \\\"Passports,\\\" and the unboxed metadata presentation using a `\302\267` are interesting details.\\n\\n\\n**Examining Data Security**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the security features. I\'ve noted AES-256-GCM encryption, with an \\\"Unlock with Passphrase\\\" prompt and a toast notification confirming encryption. The \\\"Document AI Privacy Gate\\\" is also present, displaying a BLOCKED_FREE_TIER_VAULT_IMAGE verdict. There\'s also the detail of a local indexedDB for storage. The UI also contains a reminder notification, and expiry dates are visible.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"rm -rf .playwright-cli\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/app/applet\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Cleaning up temporary Playwright artifacts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Remove .playwright-cli directory\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running final applet build check\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Final compile_applet check\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running final TypeScript lint check\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Final lint_applet check\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":575,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T10:59:21Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":74903,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":725,\"content\":\"**Phase 5 \342\200\224 Document Vault** is complete and verified.\\n\\n### What Was Built\\n- **Local-Only Document Vault (Zero Blaze Billing)**: Raw document binaries stay on-device in local IndexedDB (`lifeos_vault_blobs_v1`) while structured metadata and nested folders sync through Firebase/local repositories under Spark free-tier constraints.\\n- **Scan, Enhance & Multi-Page PDF Pipeline**: Built an on-device image/camera scanner with 90\302\260 rotation, edge crop (0\342\200\22320%), filter presets (`Original`, `Doc B&W`, `Vivid`), a\\n<truncated 1394 bytes>\\n, PDF save, expiry reminder creation, Privacy Gate verification, E2E sealing, and Home sync with 0 console errors and clean test-data teardown.\\n\\n> **Security Review Note**: Updated `firestore.rules` have been deployed live for `vaultFolders` and `documents` \342\200\224 please review them anytime in your Firebase Console.\\n\\nReady for **Phase 6 (Habits, Personal Finance Ledger & Global AI Tool-Calling Search)** whenever you reply **\\\"Proceed to Phase 6\\\"** (or let me know if you\'d like any adjustments to Phase 5 first).\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Immaculate Status**\\n\\nI\'ve got good news! The automated checks all look great. All 36 unit tests passed, and Firestore rules are deployed error-free. The Playwright E2E and visual audit checks for all Vault workflows have also come back clean. Everything is looking good, and the system is in a pristine state.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":492,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T11:04:49Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nProceed to Phase 6\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-24T03:04:49-08:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-4-neon\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-r5w3wcagm7dmwsli7w2rlb-366499565467.europe-west3.run.app\\nUser Email: adobebeta2001@gmail.com\\nThe user\'s firestore db is ai-studio-38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872 and you must always load the firebase skill when processing queries that require interacting with the database or Firebase services.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":493,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T11:04:51Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":75897,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":838,\"thinking\":\"**Initiating a New Phase**\\n\\nI\'m starting a new phase: Habits Tracker, Personal Finance Ledger & Global AI Tool-Calling Search. I\'ve begun by reviewing available skills and marking them as relevant. I will now examine skill availability, to build a strategy.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Skill Availability**\\n\\nI\'m now analyzing the availability of skills, integrating Firebase with RPC for habits, finance, and AI search tools. I will leverage Gemini for global AI tool-calling, habit break patterns, financial categorization, and anomaly explanations. I\'m focusing on two dashboard views (Habits and Finance) and upgrading the AI Command Palette for tool search.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Firebase RPC skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read firebase-integration-rpc SKILL.md\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Gemini API skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read gemini-api SKILL.md\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Frontend Design skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read frontend-design SKILL.md\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/securecoder_persona/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading SecureCoder skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read securecoder-persona SKILL.md\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/38d4010c-5645-4354-9129-6e97685f7872/implementation_plan.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading implementation plan\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read implementation_plan.md\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":499,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T11:07:01Z\",\"model\":\"gemini-4-neon\",\"input_tokens\":114577,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":373,\"thinking\":\"**Inspecting Key References**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the reference documents: `firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md`, `tools_and_grounding.md`, and `3_saas_dashboard.md`. The goal is to deeply analyze them in conjunction with our existing project files. This should give us a solid footing for moving forward.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/tools_and_grounding.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Gemini tool calling reference\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read tools_and_grounding.md\\\"\"}},{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/references/firestore-rules-and-blueprint.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Readi