    thinking: "**Discovering Existing Assets**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I found that `DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD`, `FxRatesToIqd`, and `getCrossRate` are already defined in `src/core/debts/debtSchemas.ts`. I also realize I can re-export `FxRatesToIqd` and `DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD`. Plus, I can overload `convertMinorUnits` in `src/core/currency/currency.ts` to accept `rateFromTo: number | FxRatesTo`.\n\n\n**Implementing Parallel Fixes**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the progress! Applying those six fixes in parallel is working brilliantly. Specifically, I\'ve exported the necessary items in `currency.ts` and updated the `convertMinorUnits` function. I also addressed the type definition in `server.ts`, and incorporated the \'todo\' status in the task creation. Moreover, I\'ve guarded the string joins within `globalSearchEngine.ts` and fixed the timestamps in tests. Finally, I\'ve switched over to using `res.added` and `res.currentStreak` in `HabitsView.tsx` and used the new arguments for `showToast`, and am using the new labels in `FinanceView.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "U38Fa-_kMpD0z7IPtLeZqA0"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3078416848801740707"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Export FxRatesToIqd and DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD from currency.ts and support FxRatesToIqd in convertMinorUnits\", \"EndLine\":60, \"Instruction\":\"Add FxRatesToIqd type, DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD constant, and support passing either a numeric rate or FxRatesToIqd table to convertMinorUnits\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export interface FxRatesToIqd {\\n  IQD: number;\\n  USD: number;\\n  EUR: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport const DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD: FxRatesToIqd = {\\n  IQD: 1,\\n  USD: 1500,\\n  EUR: 1620,\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Converts an amount in minor units from one currency to another using either an explicit\\n * numeric snapshot rate (units of target major per 1 unit of source major) or an FxRatesToIqd table.\\n */\\nexport function convertMinorUnits(\\n  sourceMinor: number,\\n  from: CurrencyCode,\\n  to: CurrencyCode,\\n  rateOrTable: number | FxRatesToIqd\\n): number {\\n  if (!Number.isInteger(sourceMinor)) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Source minor amount must be an integer\');\\n  }\\n  if (from === to) return sourceMinor;\\n  const rateFromTo =\\n    typeof rateOrTable === \'number\'\\n      ? rateOrTable\\n      : rateOrTable[from] / rateOrTable[to];\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(rateFromTo) || rateFromTo <= 0) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Exchange rate must be a positive finite number\');\\n  }\\n  const sourceMajor = fromMinorUnits(sourceMinor, from);\\n  return toMinorUnits(sourceMajor * rateFromTo, to);\\n}\", \"StartLine\":39, \"TargetContent\":\"/**\\n * Converts an amount in minor units from one currency to another using an explicit snapshot rate\\n * (where rate = units of target major currency per 1 unit of source major currency).\\n */\\nexport function convertMinorUnits(\\n  sourceMinor: number,\\n  from: CurrencyCode,\\n  to: CurrencyCode,\\n  rateFromTo: number\\n): number {\\n  if (!Number.isInteger(sourceMinor)) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Source minor amount must be an integer\');\\n  }\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(rateFromTo) || rateFromTo <= 0) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Exchange rate must be a positive finite number\');\\n  }\\n  if (from === to) return sourceMinor;\\n  const sourceMajor = fromMinorUnits(sourceMinor, from);\\n  return toMinorUnits(sourceMajor * rateFromTo, to);\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/core/currency/currency.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Exporting FxRatesToIqd & DEFAULT_FX_RATES_TO_IQD in currency.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/core/currency/currency.ts\"}"
